WEBVTT

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:12.721
<i>♪ Go ♪</i>

00:00:15.807 --> 00:00:18.560
<i>♪ Nothing can stop me</i>
<i>I'm all the way up ♪</i>

00:00:19.728 --> 00:00:23.482
<i>♪ All the way up</i>
<i>I'm all the way up ♪</i>

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:26.527
<i>♪ I'm all the way up ♪</i>

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.695
<i>♪ Nothing can stop me</i>
<i>I'm all the way up ♪</i>

00:00:28.779 --> 00:00:31.198
<i>♪ Shorty, what you want?</i>
<i>Shorty, what you need? ♪</i>

00:00:31.281 --> 00:00:34.117
<i>♪ My niggas run the game</i>
<i>We ain't never leavin' ♪</i>

00:00:34.201 --> 00:00:36.328
<i>♪ Countin' up this money</i>
<i>We ain't never sleepin' ♪</i>

00:00:37.538 --> 00:00:38.914
Had a big one, Dr. C?

00:00:38.997 --> 00:00:41.458
Another day, another life.

00:00:41.542 --> 00:00:43.544
-Oh, hell yeah.
-All right.

00:00:44.419 --> 00:00:45.712
<i>♪ I'm all the way up ♪</i>

00:00:46.797 --> 00:00:48.799
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

00:00:49.925 --> 00:00:50.968
Thank you.

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:55.097
And he is out. Can't feel a thing.

00:00:56.598 --> 00:00:59.518
-That's what she said. [laughing]
-[chuckling]

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:01.812
I mean, I'm good, but I can't fix that.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:05.107
Okay. Give me a 5/1 suture
on a C1 needle.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:06.650
-Stitch to cannula.
-[phone ringing]

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:07.818
Phone.

00:01:09.236 --> 00:01:11.113
-Hello?
-[man] <i>How ya doing, pal?</i>

00:01:11.196 --> 00:01:13.115
It's Kenny. You got a sec?

00:01:13.699 --> 00:01:14.700
Ah, yeah.

00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:17.160
Father of the groom. Are you psyched?

00:01:17.244 --> 00:01:19.621
-Yeah...
<i>-Look, I know you got stuff,</i>

00:01:19.705 --> 00:01:21.623
but we got a bit of a jam going on.

00:01:21.707 --> 00:01:24.876
A lot of people didn't check off
whether they want steak or fish.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.629
I was wondering if you had an idea

00:01:27.713 --> 00:01:31.425
what your side of the family
would want more.

00:01:31.508 --> 00:01:33.218
<i>Then we don't have to over-order.</i>

00:01:33.302 --> 00:01:34.970
-Uh...
-Take your time.

00:01:35.596 --> 00:01:38.849
Well, maybe a steak by a little.

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.142
Oh, that's great!

00:01:40.726 --> 00:01:42.436
-So, would you say...
-[whispers] No.

00:01:42.519 --> 00:01:45.188
<i>...maybe 60% steak, 40% fish or...</i>

00:01:45.272 --> 00:01:49.192
Uh, you know, I can still help you pay
for the wedding if you'd let me--

00:01:49.276 --> 00:01:51.320
No, no! I got this. All good here, pal.

00:01:51.403 --> 00:01:55.240
The wedding, the hotel rooms. Mmm!

00:01:55.824 --> 00:01:58.869
Yeah. Pinky Toe! Get down! Down!
Get her down!

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:00.329
<i>-She shouldn't be here.</i>
-[beeping]

00:02:00.412 --> 00:02:03.248
Uh, you know what?
Uh, could you hold on for a second?

00:02:03.332 --> 00:02:05.542
<i>Yeah, not a problem.</i>

00:02:05.626 --> 00:02:07.628
<i>No, no, no! Take her off the table.</i>

00:02:07.711 --> 00:02:10.714
<i>Because she's licking the cookies,</i>
<i>and, yes, I'll still eat them.</i>

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:11.757
[girl giggles]

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:14.885
-Hello? Ugh! Damn it!
-[line buzzing]

00:02:17.596 --> 00:02:19.723
-Hey.
-Hi!

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:22.559
Can you believe it's in five days?

00:02:22.643 --> 00:02:24.436
<i>It's like, is this really happening?</i>

00:02:24.519 --> 00:02:26.396
[giggling] I mean, in a good way!

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:27.522
Yeah, it's great.

00:02:27.606 --> 00:02:30.150
I just have one question for you
as a doctor.

00:02:30.233 --> 00:02:34.821
Um, I read about this candy being recalled
due to salmonella.

00:02:34.905 --> 00:02:37.699
<i>And I was buying candies </i>
<i>for the wedding...</i>

00:02:37.783 --> 00:02:39.409
Now I can't think of the brand.

00:02:39.493 --> 00:02:41.286
You know what? Maybe text it later.

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:46.083
It was a peppermint bark,
and also a drizzled peanut brittle.

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:48.502
<i>Very nice.</i>
<i>Me and the girls were taste-testing.</i>

00:02:48.585 --> 00:02:51.922
But now, I'm reading
salmonella could be fatal?

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:54.591
Well, actually, that's pretty rare.

00:02:55.217 --> 00:02:58.470
I mean, the only deaths I've seen reported
are children under three.

00:02:58.553 --> 00:03:02.015
Oh, thank God! Yay!
Okay, well, mine are older.

00:03:02.099 --> 00:03:05.936
So 15 is okay then, right?
Even if she got her period late?

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:09.398
What the hell are we...
Here, hand me the phone. Hi.

00:03:09.481 --> 00:03:13.652
Hey! Okay, we're done bothering you, pal.
Go back to doing whatever you were doing.

00:03:13.735 --> 00:03:15.278
Sounds good. See you.

00:03:18.657 --> 00:03:19.866
I wanna talk to you.

00:03:20.617 --> 00:03:23.328
[mother] I am so sorry
I'm such an embarrassment to you!

00:03:23.412 --> 00:03:27.165
I just wanted to know if my family
was in jeopardy from salmonella!

00:03:27.249 --> 00:03:30.127
[Kenny] You couldn't google it
like everything else you google?

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.712
[mother] So now I over-google?

00:03:31.795 --> 00:03:35.340
[Kenny] You wasted the man's time!
He's a heart doctor.

00:03:35.424 --> 00:03:38.760
-Did you not hear the beepy things?
-[mother] I know how beeps work!

00:03:38.844 --> 00:03:41.012
They were normal beeps, not long beeps!

00:03:41.096 --> 00:03:43.348
I never would've bothered him
during a long beep!

00:03:43.432 --> 00:03:45.517
-That's cute.
-[Kenny and mother continue shouting]

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.811
The toothbrush for you,
the stethoscope for Tyler.

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:48.895
You like it?

00:03:48.979 --> 00:03:53.316
-[Kenny] I'll pay. It's gonna be great.
-It was Isaac's idea.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:56.236
[mother] Of course it is!
You're an amazing father!

00:03:56.319 --> 00:03:58.905
-You're just tense!
-[Kenny] I'm not tense!

00:04:00.449 --> 00:04:03.201
Okay! Hey, everybody!

00:04:03.702 --> 00:04:07.539
<i>Grapes of Wrath,</i> Rose, good choice.
You still gotta read the book, though.

00:04:07.622 --> 00:04:09.458
-Have you read it?
-I'm gonna read it with you.

00:04:09.541 --> 00:04:12.419
Tyler, you're gonna take him to practice?
That's not gonna stress you out?

00:04:12.502 --> 00:04:13.712
-Yeah, no big deal.
-All right.

00:04:13.795 --> 00:04:15.797
I'm gonna go to the airport
and pick up Seymour.

00:04:15.881 --> 00:04:18.049
-Who's that?
-He's Dad's grand-uncle.

00:04:18.133 --> 00:04:19.926
He's the oldest living Lustig.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:23.597
Come on. You met him in Miami.
He's got all those great stories?

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:25.140
He's got one leg?

00:04:25.223 --> 00:04:27.684
-Oh, right.
-Yeah, you're gonna love him.

00:04:27.768 --> 00:04:29.978
What are you doing?
Why're you walking like this?

00:04:30.061 --> 00:04:32.314
-Are they too tight?
-No, my feet are swollen.

00:04:32.397 --> 00:04:36.318
-I'll go to Penney's. I'll return them.
-No, they fit. I'm just breaking them in.

00:04:36.401 --> 00:04:38.987
It's so she doesn't walk like that
at the wedding, Mr. Lustig.

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:41.615
-Okay. What's my favorite candy bar?
-The Whatchamacallit.

00:04:41.698 --> 00:04:43.408
-Who's my favorite first daughter?
-Me.

00:04:43.492 --> 00:04:44.826
-I love you.
-Love you. Bye.

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:47.120
-I love you.
-Thank you, Mr. Lustig.

00:04:47.204 --> 00:04:50.207
[Billy Joel's "Scenes
from an Italian Restaurant" playing]

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:53.043
{\an8}[sportscaster speaking indistinctly
on radio]

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:56.296
<i>But give me a reason</i>
<i>to want to watch a Met game. I mean...</i>

00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:01.134
{\an8}Here they come.

00:05:06.598 --> 00:05:09.768
-Seymour!
-[grumbling]<i> </i>Hi.

00:05:09.851 --> 00:05:13.188
-[man] You got him from here?
-Oh, you're not his nurse?

00:05:13.271 --> 00:05:15.732
Sir, I work for the airline.
I'm not a nurse.

00:05:15.816 --> 00:05:18.485
What? No, I was saying
because of the wheelchair--

00:05:18.568 --> 00:05:21.696
This is an airport wheelchair.
And I'm actually gonna need it back.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:23.156
Someone needs it more, sir.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:27.744
Oh! Someone needs it more than this guy?
Okay. Okay.

00:05:29.079 --> 00:05:30.831
-How was your trip?
-[Seymour grumbles]

00:05:34.417 --> 00:05:35.293
[Kenny] Oh.

00:05:39.506 --> 00:05:41.424
-Oh. Oh!
-[Seymour grunting]

00:05:42.259 --> 00:05:43.218
Sorry.

00:05:44.511 --> 00:05:45.679
What?

00:05:46.263 --> 00:05:48.640
-[Kenny] <i>No legs?</i>
-Yeah. Why?

00:05:48.723 --> 00:05:52.477
I thought he still had one.
You didn't tell me.

00:05:52.561 --> 00:05:55.605
Well, maybe you never asked.
That's diabetes. Works fast.

00:05:55.689 --> 00:05:56.982
<i>-Terrible.</i>
-Yeah.

00:05:57.566 --> 00:05:59.025
Anything else? I'm at work.

00:05:59.109 --> 00:06:01.611
Okay. Why is he alone?

00:06:01.695 --> 00:06:03.780
What, you think I got time
to come in early?

00:06:03.864 --> 00:06:06.616
World doesn't stop, bud.
I'm running a pharmacy here.

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:09.077
Look, call me later
and I'll give you the instructions.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:11.454
[Kenny] Instructions? What instructions?

00:06:11.538 --> 00:06:14.207
You know, changing, his upkeep,
all that stuff.

00:06:14.291 --> 00:06:16.877
-So, he doesn't have a nurse?
-Oh, calm down!

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:19.462
The doc says he can go 48 hours
without another cleaning

00:06:19.546 --> 00:06:21.673
<i>-if you don't have time.</i>
-What's a "cleaning"?

00:06:21.756 --> 00:06:23.425
-We'll talk. I got a customer.
<i>-Wait!</i>

00:06:23.508 --> 00:06:26.136
So, he's gonna stay
at the hotel all alone?

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:29.055
You're putting him in a hotel? He's 87!

00:06:29.139 --> 00:06:32.601
It's just, there's so much going on
at the house already--

00:06:32.684 --> 00:06:34.102
The man is 87!

00:06:34.185 --> 00:06:36.146
[Kenny] Okay, I'm taking him home!

00:06:36.229 --> 00:06:39.232
[Billy Joel's "Scenes
from an Italian Restaurant" playing]

00:06:40.609 --> 00:06:44.696
Oh, so, how's the painting going, Seymour?
You still doing the ceramics?

00:06:44.779 --> 00:06:45.614
No.

00:07:01.296 --> 00:07:07.510
Just tell Sarah to help you.
Move my desk and fold out the sofa.

00:07:07.594 --> 00:07:10.388
[mother] <i>You were gonna put him</i>
<i>in a hotel? With no legs?</i>

00:07:10.472 --> 00:07:12.599
I didn't know about the no legs!

00:07:12.682 --> 00:07:14.976
[scoffs] <i>It's fine. It's one person.</i>

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:18.605
Yes. Um, just... I'll be another hour.

00:07:18.688 --> 00:07:21.816
Tell everyone to meet at the house,
not the hotel.

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:25.403
[man] Our condos get divorced dads
who wanna be near their kids.

00:07:25.487 --> 00:07:27.822
They wanna feel like
they're living in a nice place.

00:07:27.906 --> 00:07:29.658
Yeah. We can do that. Absolutely.

00:07:29.741 --> 00:07:33.161
Easy to accommodate.
Not high-end, but very nice.

00:07:33.244 --> 00:07:34.871
Would you like to see some of our work?

00:07:34.955 --> 00:07:37.540
-Uh, well, Norman--
-I'm Kenny. Norman's my boss.

00:07:37.624 --> 00:07:39.000
Right, sorry.

00:07:39.084 --> 00:07:42.545
There's a Quality Lodge in Mineola
that we upgraded last year.

00:07:42.629 --> 00:07:46.633
Took it to a Two Diamond from Triple A.
This is almost unheard of.

00:07:46.716 --> 00:07:49.302
Uh, my daughter's
getting married there Saturday.

00:07:49.386 --> 00:07:52.430
Really? You're having a wedding
at a Quality Lodge?

00:07:52.514 --> 00:07:54.099
It's a Two Diamond.

00:07:56.142 --> 00:07:59.729
I only have a half an hour, but let me
get my car and we'll go for a drive--

00:07:59.813 --> 00:08:00.855
Let me drive you.

00:08:00.939 --> 00:08:04.025
We're a smaller company,
which is a positive.

00:08:04.109 --> 00:08:05.735
I get to be hands-on this way.

00:08:05.819 --> 00:08:08.905
I'll be there through the completion
of the entire project--

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:16.246
-Hey! You're up!
-Where'd you go?

00:08:16.329 --> 00:08:20.000
This is my uncle, Seymour.
He just flew in from Florida.

00:08:20.625 --> 00:08:23.294
You were asleep, buddy.
I didn't wanna wake you.

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:26.548
He was asleep.

00:08:26.631 --> 00:08:29.509
The rec center over there,
they went with us.

00:08:29.592 --> 00:08:31.594
Did the piping in the locker room.

00:08:31.678 --> 00:08:34.556
And updated the alarm system
in that building.

00:08:34.639 --> 00:08:35.598
I gotta go.

00:08:36.474 --> 00:08:38.309
We're almost home, Seymour.

00:08:38.393 --> 00:08:40.020
-Bathroom.
-Oh.

00:08:41.271 --> 00:08:45.275
We're almost done, okay?
Don't you have your pull-ups on?

00:08:45.358 --> 00:08:47.819
That's for piss, this is a shitting.

00:08:49.779 --> 00:08:52.991
Just about where we have to be.
Can you hold it in for four minutes?

00:08:53.074 --> 00:08:54.075
I can't.

00:08:55.744 --> 00:08:57.203
It's three minutes now.

00:08:58.163 --> 00:08:59.622
I can give you two.

00:09:02.834 --> 00:09:04.586
What happened? What happened?

00:09:04.669 --> 00:09:06.546
Oh, now it folds.

00:09:06.629 --> 00:09:08.298
Are you kidding me?

00:09:08.965 --> 00:09:11.676
[panting] I've never used
one of these before.

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:13.011
What's taking so long?

00:09:13.094 --> 00:09:14.387
[chuckling] Seymour...

00:09:15.805 --> 00:09:18.349
Let's... Let's get... Let's get...
Let's go.

00:09:19.392 --> 00:09:20.643
This is actually a good thing,

00:09:20.727 --> 00:09:23.521
because they have Dyson Airblade
hand dryers,

00:09:23.605 --> 00:09:24.731
which I can show you.

00:09:24.814 --> 00:09:27.859
-It'd be good for your lobby bathrooms.
-[man] Uh-huh.

00:09:28.276 --> 00:09:30.195
There's no, uh, handicapped room?

00:09:30.278 --> 00:09:33.698
No, I did not say that.
Well, put him on the phone, then.

00:09:34.574 --> 00:09:37.494
Isaac, did you tell your mom
I said not to shower?

00:09:37.827 --> 00:09:41.790
I did not-- Because your mother says
your fingernails are filthy!

00:09:42.582 --> 00:09:45.418
They're both 23 years old.
Feels young to me.

00:09:46.544 --> 00:09:49.964
But they're in love, I guess.
So, who knows what's right.

00:09:50.048 --> 00:09:52.926
-Mm-hmm.
-[Seymour grunting]

00:09:56.012 --> 00:09:59.224
Nobody told me about the no legs at all.

00:10:03.103 --> 00:10:05.855
-Oh, somebody's in there.
-Don't see anybody.

00:10:05.939 --> 00:10:07.357
[Seymour] Okay, I'm done.

00:10:09.901 --> 00:10:11.653
[man 2 sighs]

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:14.197
I'm ready!

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:15.740
[clears throat]

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:30.421
[Seymour] Need those baby wipes.

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:34.717
[mother] They both picked Tufts
so they could live together.

00:10:34.801 --> 00:10:36.845
She's in dental, he's in med.

00:10:36.928 --> 00:10:41.683
Okay. Good for him. I thought
he was just gonna be a dentist, too.

00:10:41.766 --> 00:10:44.769
There's a lot of great dentists
out there, Iris.

00:10:44.853 --> 00:10:48.481
Not all of them fondle people
when they're under the gas.

00:10:48.565 --> 00:10:49.691
All right, Ma.

00:10:49.774 --> 00:10:53.528
You guys, wait till you see Sarah's dress.
I've seen her in it. It's so beyond.

00:10:53.611 --> 00:10:55.446
Tasteful, not whore-y at all.

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:57.824
I still wish you would've worn mine.

00:10:57.907 --> 00:10:59.409
I'm sorry, Grandma, I know. I just--

00:10:59.492 --> 00:11:00.994
She's wearing her own dress!

00:11:01.077 --> 00:11:03.830
[chuckling] You guys, I said I saw it.

00:11:03.913 --> 00:11:06.833
And look at Isaac! Oh, my God.

00:11:06.916 --> 00:11:10.003
I just wanna squeeze this head
till it explodes!

00:11:10.086 --> 00:11:14.090
Oh, I could just pull his face off
and put it on my night table,

00:11:14.174 --> 00:11:16.426
so I could see it before I go to bed!

00:11:16.509 --> 00:11:19.679
You should've seen this one in the play.
He was phenomenal.

00:11:19.762 --> 00:11:21.431
He was the only one you looked at.

00:11:21.514 --> 00:11:23.433
Wait a minute. This is amazing.

00:11:23.516 --> 00:11:26.060
He was in a Broadway play?

00:11:26.144 --> 00:11:28.021
No. In camp.

00:11:28.104 --> 00:11:30.231
Oh, was it Juilliard camp?

00:11:30.315 --> 00:11:31.399
No.

00:11:31.482 --> 00:11:33.943
Was it a camp for theatrical children?

00:11:34.819 --> 00:11:35.862
No.

00:11:36.446 --> 00:11:38.448
It wasn't a special ed camp?

00:11:39.449 --> 00:11:41.159
No. It wasn't.

00:11:41.242 --> 00:11:42.744
Oh, thank God.

00:11:42.827 --> 00:11:45.663
-Hey, hey! Here he is! The man himself.
-[all chattering excitedly]

00:11:46.956 --> 00:11:48.499
What are you doing?

00:11:48.583 --> 00:11:52.128
If anyone can figure out how to open up
the wheelchair out front, please!

00:11:52.212 --> 00:11:54.714
-Put my brother down!
-I will, Iris.

00:11:54.797 --> 00:11:56.090
Can somebody get a chair?

00:11:56.174 --> 00:11:59.010
This is my little girl,
the one who's getting married.

00:11:59.093 --> 00:12:01.429
Hi, Uncle Seymour.
Thank you so much for coming in.

00:12:01.512 --> 00:12:03.765
-[Seymour grumbles]
-[Kenny] And little Rose.

00:12:03.848 --> 00:12:05.266
I thought he had one leg.

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:07.185
No, he has less.

00:12:07.268 --> 00:12:10.230
Okay, give him a kiss, sweetie. That's it.

00:12:10.313 --> 00:12:12.398
Isaac, give your uncle a kiss.

00:12:12.482 --> 00:12:13.524
I-I, I did.

00:12:13.608 --> 00:12:16.861
[Kenny] Okay, then let's sit down here.

00:12:16.945 --> 00:12:21.699
Here you go, Seymour. That's it.
That's it, we're in there.

00:12:21.783 --> 00:12:26.871
Seymour, Seymour, it's Roberta.
How are you?

00:12:26.955 --> 00:12:29.249
I'm okay now. Finally.

00:12:29.332 --> 00:12:32.001
He put me in a car
with no air conditioning.

00:12:32.085 --> 00:12:35.630
-Treated me like a dog.
-[Iris and Roberta chattering]

00:12:35.713 --> 00:12:37.590
Isaac likes Jeremy Lin?

00:12:37.674 --> 00:12:41.261
And he's aware that Jeremy Lin
no longer plays for the New York Knicks?

00:12:41.344 --> 00:12:44.055
It's a very nice shirt, $7 at Modell's.

00:12:45.306 --> 00:12:46.557
-We're so late.
-Right.

00:12:46.641 --> 00:12:49.769
-I'm so sorry. Hi.
-Never too late. How are ya?

00:12:49.852 --> 00:12:52.522
Had to come see the man of the hour!

00:12:52.605 --> 00:12:54.482
[indistinct chatter]

00:12:54.565 --> 00:12:56.567
Eighty-seven years old!

00:12:58.278 --> 00:13:00.822
-[Jared] Mr. Lustig?
-That's right.

00:13:00.905 --> 00:13:02.407
[all laughing]

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:04.367
Why did we invite them, again?

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:06.411
They're our neighbors. We had to.

00:13:06.494 --> 00:13:08.788
He just gets so weird with me.

00:13:08.871 --> 00:13:11.457
You've known them all your life.
There's pictures of you as babies!

00:13:11.541 --> 00:13:13.668
-He still has them up in his room.
-Yeah.

00:13:13.751 --> 00:13:16.004
We are late because
Jared had a singing lesson.

00:13:16.087 --> 00:13:16.921
[mother] Oh, Jared.

00:13:17.005 --> 00:13:18.840
[Roberta] You could do something
at the wedding.

00:13:18.923 --> 00:13:22.051
What was the one you sang at her Sweet 16?

00:13:22.135 --> 00:13:23.886
That was a Ray LaMontagne.

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:26.264
But that was kind of our song.

00:13:26.848 --> 00:13:29.684
-[Roberta and Iris] Aw!
-Well, that's ancient history.

00:13:29.767 --> 00:13:34.147
Perfect. So maybe you could do
one of his songs with the band.

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:35.690
It's not a band, it's a DJ.

00:13:35.773 --> 00:13:37.358
Sarah's cousin Jeddy.

00:13:37.442 --> 00:13:40.278
He's supposed to be incredible.
Kid's a whiz.

00:13:40.361 --> 00:13:41.654
He's 12 years old.

00:13:41.738 --> 00:13:45.241
Oh, and the father-daughter song.
We gotta pick one, kiddo.

00:13:45.325 --> 00:13:48.453
Think about Billy Joel.
I used to sing it to you as a kid, huh?

00:13:48.536 --> 00:13:50.371
-Okay.
-All right. See you in a little bit.

00:13:50.455 --> 00:13:54.917
Kenny. Kenny. I was telling Seymour
that the other father's rich.

00:13:55.001 --> 00:13:58.171
He's a surgeon.
Why didn't you let him pay for the band?

00:13:58.921 --> 00:14:00.965
We're fine, Iris. The kid's a whiz.

00:14:01.049 --> 00:14:03.968
[Billy Joel's "Scenes
from an Italian Restaurant" playing]

00:14:04.093 --> 00:14:06.512
[sportscaster speaking indistinctly
over radio]

00:14:09.349 --> 00:14:11.893
I just gotta make sure
the groom's dad is happy.

00:14:11.976 --> 00:14:13.770
He's very, very...

00:14:15.313 --> 00:14:18.232
-This is the Executive Suite?
-[chuckling] Yes, yes.

00:14:19.859 --> 00:14:21.527
Do you have any bigger ones?

00:14:21.611 --> 00:14:24.864
No, no. This Executive Suite.

00:14:26.157 --> 00:14:27.158
I know. I...

00:14:27.825 --> 00:14:31.204
Maybe wondering if we can do something
to jazz it up.

00:14:31.287 --> 00:14:33.373
If you got anything leather.

00:14:34.582 --> 00:14:37.960
Old, uh, ottoman from old room.

00:14:38.711 --> 00:14:40.088
We keep one in basement.

00:14:40.171 --> 00:14:41.422
Okay. Good.

00:14:41.506 --> 00:14:47.220
What else? Maybe something...
More gadgets or high-techy stuff or--

00:14:47.303 --> 00:14:48.221
I will look.

00:14:49.097 --> 00:14:51.724
-There is toaster.
-Okay. You'll look.

00:14:51.808 --> 00:14:55.395
Oh! I got an old chandelier in my attic.

00:14:55.478 --> 00:14:58.481
You can install it
or I can get you one of my guys.

00:14:58.564 --> 00:14:59.732
We can do.

00:14:59.816 --> 00:15:01.984
You're the best, Hanan. Now we're cookin'.

00:15:02.068 --> 00:15:04.320
Let's keep thinking, come up with more.

00:15:04.404 --> 00:15:07.281
And we are not ever gonna tell anybody

00:15:07.365 --> 00:15:10.159
that this stuff
wasn't already in the room, right?

00:15:10.243 --> 00:15:12.245
[chuckling] Yes. Okay.

00:15:12.829 --> 00:15:14.455
Hey, how about this?

00:15:14.539 --> 00:15:16.374
How about we put a sign on, like...

00:15:16.541 --> 00:15:19.502
"Governor's Suite"
or "Thomas Jefferson Suite"?

00:15:19.585 --> 00:15:22.046
Can you do that quick?
Can you get that up by Wednesday?

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:23.548
[chuckling] Yes. Yes.

00:15:23.631 --> 00:15:25.466
Yeah. All right. All right.

00:15:30.430 --> 00:15:32.306
[mother] Don't write "doctor"
on that card.

00:15:32.390 --> 00:15:35.435
He's just a chiropractor,
so make it "mister," okay?

00:15:35.518 --> 00:15:36.394
-[Rose] Okay.
-Hey.

00:15:36.477 --> 00:15:38.938
Oh, hey. How was the hotel?

00:15:39.021 --> 00:15:42.191
Perfect. It's all set. What has happened?
Why you guys up?

00:15:42.275 --> 00:15:44.652
We couldn't finish the name tags
'cause everyone stayed late.

00:15:44.735 --> 00:15:47.113
Yeah, so now we're gonna have to
rush the calligraphy.

00:15:47.196 --> 00:15:48.948
Sarah, you should've eloped
like Mom and Dad.

00:15:49.031 --> 00:15:50.867
-[Sarah] Nice.
-What's an "elope"?

00:15:51.534 --> 00:15:54.162
[stammering] It's when you sneak off
and get married in secret.

00:15:54.245 --> 00:15:56.539
Yeah, we lived with our parents
for four months.

00:15:56.622 --> 00:15:58.833
We were too afraid to tell them.
[laughing]

00:15:58.916 --> 00:16:00.334
You lied to your parents?

00:16:00.418 --> 00:16:02.712
-[Kenny] No, it never came up.
-It was a different time.

00:16:02.795 --> 00:16:05.381
I think it's romantic
that Dad couldn't wait to marry Mom.

00:16:05.465 --> 00:16:08.342
I was lucky.
Hey, come on. We gotta go to sleep.

00:16:08.426 --> 00:16:09.844
-Did you brush?
-[Isaac] Yeah.

00:16:09.927 --> 00:16:11.762
-Let me smell.
-[Isaac exhales]

00:16:11.846 --> 00:16:13.181
He's not lying. He did it.

00:16:13.264 --> 00:16:16.267
For the first time, he told the truth,
but let's go to sleep, guys.

00:16:16.350 --> 00:16:17.935
I don't want you
to be cranky tomorrow.

00:16:18.019 --> 00:16:21.314
I'm begging you. Seymour's...
I don't want you to wake Seymour.

00:16:21.397 --> 00:16:23.608
He seems pretty knocked out to me.

00:16:23.691 --> 00:16:26.068
No, but we gotta be considerate.
Come on. Please?

00:16:26.152 --> 00:16:27.487
No, listen. I don't need to sleep.

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:29.822
I'm gonna stretch Sarah's shoes, okay?
I'll be fine.

00:16:29.906 --> 00:16:31.157
[Kenny] You're crazy.

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:35.578
Pinky Toe. Come here, come here.
Come here, come here. All right.

00:16:36.329 --> 00:16:38.247
[Seymour groans] God damn!

00:16:38.331 --> 00:16:40.082
-What are you doing?
-Oh, shit.

00:16:40.166 --> 00:16:44.337
-What was that? Was that his head?
-Just go to sleep. Come on. Don't laugh.

00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:46.422
[whispering]

00:16:55.097 --> 00:16:56.098
[Rose] Daddy?

00:16:57.850 --> 00:17:00.394
[whispering] What? What're you doing up?

00:17:00.478 --> 00:17:02.396
I'm just worried about the wedding.

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:05.483
Hey. I get it, hon.

00:17:05.566 --> 00:17:09.028
Your sister's too young,
but this is what she wants to do.

00:17:09.111 --> 00:17:10.238
We got to accept it.

00:17:10.696 --> 00:17:14.408
Oh, no. I was worried
whether it's gonna be nice enough.

00:17:14.492 --> 00:17:15.368
What?

00:17:15.451 --> 00:17:17.411
Well, Sarah has really good taste.

00:17:17.495 --> 00:17:20.623
I mean, she's understated,
but also sophisticated.

00:17:20.706 --> 00:17:22.416
-So I don't know if a DJ--
-Okay.

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:25.378
-She didn't say these things to me.
-She knows it's important to you.

00:17:25.461 --> 00:17:30.967
Right, I'm aware about her taste, okay?
I'm on it, the whole taste thing.

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:33.344
Just... Why don't you go to sleep?
You got school.

00:17:33.427 --> 00:17:34.720
School's over. It's summer.

00:17:34.804 --> 00:17:37.682
Well, just sleep now, okay?
It's good for you.

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:43.187
[mother laughing] Oh, my God,
the three-hour difference!

00:17:43.271 --> 00:17:45.773
That's a big brain fart for me.
[chuckling]

00:17:47.275 --> 00:17:51.529
Oh, sorry! Senior moment and I'm only 48.
Can you believe it?

00:17:52.113 --> 00:17:53.656
It's okay. Um...

00:17:54.198 --> 00:17:56.325
Maybe we could talk a bit later?

00:17:56.409 --> 00:17:57.868
[mother] Sure, sure.

00:17:57.952 --> 00:18:01.455
I just thought it'd be nice to chat
before the wedding and all the craziness.

00:18:01.539 --> 00:18:02.957
Get to know each other a little.

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:05.334
Okay, so let's talk--

00:18:05.418 --> 00:18:07.003
So, all I really know is

00:18:07.086 --> 00:18:10.590
you're very pretty
and your husband wasn't around much.

00:18:10.673 --> 00:18:11.882
He played around a lot.

00:18:13.759 --> 00:18:16.262
-[whispering] What?
-[mouthing] Are you out of your mind?

00:18:16.345 --> 00:18:18.097
I am not a lip-reader.

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:21.434
-Hang the phone up. Say goodbye.
-Hello?

00:18:21.517 --> 00:18:25.479
[mother] I just wanted to ask how close
she wanted her table to the father!

00:18:25.563 --> 00:18:27.607
You have to make small talk first!

00:18:27.690 --> 00:18:29.609
[Kenny] At 4:00 in the morning!

00:18:29.692 --> 00:18:30.985
[mother] I didn't know!

00:18:31.068 --> 00:18:33.070
[Kenny] You didn't, then you did!

00:18:33.154 --> 00:18:36.240
[mother] What? I was about to get off
before you butted in!

00:18:36.324 --> 00:18:38.951
[Kenny] You know something?
I can't die first!

00:18:39.035 --> 00:18:40.745
I know it's wrong to say,

00:18:40.828 --> 00:18:44.665
but I couldn't handle you
ever making decisions all by yourself!

00:18:44.749 --> 00:18:47.501
It wouldn't be fair to you or the kids!

00:18:47.585 --> 00:18:51.047
[Roberta] Sweetheart, you need to
gain weight. You're too skinny.

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:52.465
There you go, darling.

00:18:52.548 --> 00:18:55.301
-Okay, all right. Looking good. Open.
-Ah!

00:18:55.384 --> 00:18:57.470
-Oh, yeah.
-Such service!

00:18:57.553 --> 00:19:01.015
Anybody figure out the chair?
The button situation?

00:19:01.098 --> 00:19:03.309
[muffled] Good morning, Seymour.

00:19:03.392 --> 00:19:05.311
Seymour, you're here. You're good.
Go ahead.

00:19:05.394 --> 00:19:08.314
Eggs, Ma, eggs.
Hey, all right. Love you, pal. Love you.

00:19:08.397 --> 00:19:09.899
-Dad?
-Yeah, what?

00:19:09.982 --> 00:19:13.277
Is Mom gonna die soon
like you were yelling about?

00:19:13.361 --> 00:19:14.695
What's that, buddy?

00:19:14.779 --> 00:19:16.864
You were deciding who to die first?

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:19.450
Oh, no, no, no.

00:19:19.533 --> 00:19:22.536
That's not gonna happen
for a very long time, pal.

00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:24.830
I was just saying that,
when it does happen,

00:19:24.914 --> 00:19:28.292
I think it would be best
that it's your mom, for everyone's sake.

00:19:28.376 --> 00:19:31.420
Okay, guys.
I'm sorry to break up all the fun.

00:19:31.504 --> 00:19:33.964
I have to stop by work.
That's what the boxes are for.

00:19:34.048 --> 00:19:36.634
Seymour, Seymour,
you need to go to the bathroom?

00:19:36.717 --> 00:19:38.594
[man] Kenny's leaving,
so now is the time.

00:19:38.678 --> 00:19:40.012
[Seymour] Not now.

00:19:40.096 --> 00:19:42.098
-[Iris] Why don't you just try?
-[Seymour] No.

00:19:42.181 --> 00:19:44.016
[Roberta] You sure
you don't have to make?

00:19:44.100 --> 00:19:45.935
[mother] Norman gave you
the rest of the week off.

00:19:46.018 --> 00:19:48.604
Oh, he did. I just...
I'm gonna go by for a minute,

00:19:48.688 --> 00:19:51.065
then I'm gonna pick your brother's
family up at the airport.

00:19:51.148 --> 00:19:54.151
Okay, well, if you take the minivan,
don't adjust the seat setting.

00:19:54.235 --> 00:19:57.196
-Don't adjust it?
-No, I got it set perfect. Please!

00:19:57.279 --> 00:19:59.198
-[pop music playing over radio]
<i>-♪ This is all ♪</i>

00:19:59.323 --> 00:20:01.409
<i>♪ Brand-new to me ♪</i>

00:20:02.034 --> 00:20:04.495
[sportscaster over radio]
<i>The lineup is gonna be different.</i>

00:20:06.247 --> 00:20:08.666
Oh! Hey, hey, big man.
What's in the boxes?

00:20:08.749 --> 00:20:10.543
Oh, these? These are for him.

00:20:10.626 --> 00:20:14.296
Hi. Okay, okay.
How're we doing? How're we doing?

00:20:14.380 --> 00:20:18.092
Everybody, everybody,
this is my almost dad-in-law, Kenny.

00:20:18.175 --> 00:20:19.468
Look at this.

00:20:19.552 --> 00:20:22.304
I am so happy you made it.
Congratulations.

00:20:22.388 --> 00:20:25.349
You got quite a cousin here
or whatever he is to you.

00:20:25.433 --> 00:20:27.017
Nice to meet you.

00:20:27.101 --> 00:20:29.770
I hope everybody likes the hotel.
It's a Two Diamond.

00:20:31.188 --> 00:20:34.775
So, yeah, my company worked on it,
and it's fantastic.

00:20:34.859 --> 00:20:36.569
If you have any problems, call me.

00:20:36.652 --> 00:20:39.155
I left an emergency contact number
in every room.

00:20:39.238 --> 00:20:40.072
Hey, no problem.

00:20:40.197 --> 00:20:42.783
-Psyched to be in New York City.
-[all exclaim]

00:20:42.867 --> 00:20:45.536
Capital of the world, y'all! [laughing]

00:20:45.619 --> 00:20:47.163
Actually, we're in Long Island,

00:20:47.246 --> 00:20:50.124
which is an hour and 20 from the city.
Three hours with traffic.

00:20:50.875 --> 00:20:54.336
Probably not gonna have time for that,
but next time you come, for sure.

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:56.297
-Yeah.
-Your father, is he here?

00:20:56.380 --> 00:20:58.799
No, he's actually coming in tomorrow.

00:20:58.883 --> 00:21:02.136
-You know, work, work, work, right?
-Looking forward to meeting the man.

00:21:02.219 --> 00:21:08.017
Uh, room service is open till ten o'clock.
So enjoy that, guys. Great to meet you!

00:21:08.100 --> 00:21:12.104
I played Linus and Sarah was Lucy.
That was tenth grade.

00:21:12.188 --> 00:21:15.024
I remember that show. You were very good.
Wasn't he, Sarah?

00:21:15.107 --> 00:21:18.652
They would rehearse right in her bedroom,
for hours on end!

00:21:18.736 --> 00:21:20.362
Is that all you did?

00:21:20.446 --> 00:21:25.826
Oh, stop it, Iris. Please!
It's ancient history, just like he said.

00:21:25.910 --> 00:21:27.328
Oh, yeah, definitely.

00:21:27.411 --> 00:21:30.581
Jesus Christ, he is so pathetic.
I can't stand him.

00:21:30.664 --> 00:21:33.542
He just won't leave.
His parents aren't even here now.

00:21:33.626 --> 00:21:36.003
Do you want me to bang him?
'Cause I would totally bang him

00:21:36.086 --> 00:21:38.255
if it would help just get him away
for a while.

00:21:38.339 --> 00:21:39.673
It's okay.

00:21:39.757 --> 00:21:40.883
Think about it.

00:21:40.966 --> 00:21:43.177
So we have to decide what song
you're gonna come out to.

00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:44.261
I know.

00:21:44.345 --> 00:21:46.722
It's like, we gotta do choreography,
we have to--

00:21:46.806 --> 00:21:48.766
[screaming] Oh, my God!

00:21:49.391 --> 00:21:50.810
[greeting excitedly]

00:21:50.893 --> 00:21:53.813
Um, my number four premolar
is a little sensitive to cold.

00:21:53.896 --> 00:21:56.565
-Can you help me?
-I'm so happy you're here.

00:21:56.649 --> 00:21:59.443
Of course. Are you calm?
Have you been reading <i>Bad Feminist?</i>

00:21:59.527 --> 00:22:02.321
Yes, thank you, and I feel like
a better bad feminist for it.

00:22:02.404 --> 00:22:04.698
-[laughing]
-Hi, I'm Robin.

00:22:04.782 --> 00:22:07.076
-Oh, hi.
-My BFF.

00:22:07.159 --> 00:22:09.036
This is Emily and Danielle from school.

00:22:09.119 --> 00:22:11.789
-Hi, we've heard so much about you.
-Yes. So many stories.

00:22:11.872 --> 00:22:14.792
It's so nice to meet you two.
It's good you're here.

00:22:14.875 --> 00:22:16.544
This one could use some love right now.

00:22:16.627 --> 00:22:18.128
Oh, no.

00:22:18.212 --> 00:22:20.714
It's nothing,
especially with you guys here early.

00:22:20.798 --> 00:22:22.216
[chattering excitedly]

00:22:23.926 --> 00:22:26.720
-You are so tall in those shoes.
-[Sarah] Aw.

00:22:26.804 --> 00:22:30.516
Guys, I've seen her in her dress already.
She is gorgeous

00:22:30.599 --> 00:22:32.852
and she was just
so worried to me about it.

00:22:32.935 --> 00:22:34.186
Aw, I can't wait to see it.

00:22:34.270 --> 00:22:37.106
Oh, so we were talking
about the reception

00:22:37.231 --> 00:22:39.483
and what song we should come out to
when we're introduced.

00:22:39.567 --> 00:22:42.069
Oh, like one of those corny YouTube thing?

00:22:42.152 --> 00:22:44.530
-[Danielle] It'll be fun.
-Right?

00:22:44.613 --> 00:22:50.244
Um, so, our friend Kelly suggested
"Party Rock," LMFAO.

00:22:50.327 --> 00:22:53.622
-Oh, that's lively.
-But I suggested Journey.

00:22:53.706 --> 00:22:55.624
You know, "Don't Stop Believin'"?

00:22:55.708 --> 00:22:58.168
My God, that is perfect.

00:22:58.252 --> 00:22:59.879
[laughing] See?

00:22:59.962 --> 00:23:02.798
It's so obvious and so amazingly overdone.

00:23:02.882 --> 00:23:05.342
-Yeah, that would be hilarious.
-[giggling]

00:23:05.426 --> 00:23:07.928
[Emily] That's a good one, Robin.

00:23:08.012 --> 00:23:10.890
[sportscaster 1 over radio]
<i>Showing us that he can play center field.</i>

00:23:10.973 --> 00:23:13.934
-[sportscaster 2] <i>He's doing a good job.</i>
-[sportscaster 1] <i>He's okay.</i>

00:23:14.018 --> 00:23:16.896
<i>And obviously, I mean,</i>
<i>he's starting to hit again.</i>

00:23:20.232 --> 00:23:22.985
Mmm. I can't believe
she's getting married.

00:23:23.068 --> 00:23:25.321
I remember when you used to drive her
on her paper route

00:23:25.404 --> 00:23:27.573
'cause she was afraid to ride her bike
in the street.

00:23:27.656 --> 00:23:28.657
Yeah.

00:23:28.741 --> 00:23:32.328
Jeddy's so excited to DJ the wedding.
Aren't you, Jeddy?

00:23:32.411 --> 00:23:35.205
I hear you're quite the DJ, young man.

00:23:35.289 --> 00:23:38.334
They said he had to do it.
So you could save money.

00:23:38.417 --> 00:23:40.336
Come on, Noah. No, he doesn't mean that.

00:23:40.419 --> 00:23:41.795
Yes, he does.

00:23:41.879 --> 00:23:44.840
Oh, listen. You don't have to do it
if you don't want to.

00:23:44.924 --> 00:23:46.550
He wants to do it.

00:23:46.634 --> 00:23:49.261
I don't! Not at some stupid wedding!

00:23:49.345 --> 00:23:51.472
Noah! You see what you did?

00:23:52.973 --> 00:23:54.183
Thanks for having Noah.

00:23:54.266 --> 00:23:56.727
It's so nice
they let him out of rehab for the week.

00:23:56.810 --> 00:23:59.355
Oh, yeah. Gotta have Noah. Love the boy.

00:24:00.147 --> 00:24:03.734
Yeah. They said he can stay at your house
with special instructions.

00:24:04.610 --> 00:24:08.489
Wait, you're staying with us?
I mean, 'cause that's phenomenal.

00:24:08.572 --> 00:24:09.865
I told you that.

00:24:09.949 --> 00:24:12.368
I know you did. I know you did.

00:24:12.451 --> 00:24:16.246
I'm gonna call home, make sure
that everything is perfect for you.

00:24:16.330 --> 00:24:18.791
How're we supposed to have them here?
Please, fill me in.

00:24:18.874 --> 00:24:22.711
Yeah, so they'll stay
in Isaac's room. Right?

00:24:22.795 --> 00:24:26.215
And Isaac will move to Rose's room.
[stammering] That's great.

00:24:26.298 --> 00:24:31.595
Yeah, but Noah? How did this happen?
Did Jay tell you and you forgot about it?

00:24:32.471 --> 00:24:35.724
Yes, yes. It's gonna be great.

00:24:35.808 --> 00:24:37.851
[sighing] I gotta go.

00:24:37.935 --> 00:24:39.019
[call disconnects]

00:24:40.521 --> 00:24:44.108
Right. Of course. Yeah, sure, sure.

00:24:44.817 --> 00:24:49.571
Ah, not as excited as these guys are, huh?

00:24:50.114 --> 00:24:53.200
[chuckles] Yeah, no, we'll be home soon.
The traffic's not so bad.

00:24:53.283 --> 00:24:54.702
-[phone ringing]
-I love--

00:24:56.495 --> 00:25:01.667
What is the, uh... What's happening?
The... Is she still...

00:25:02.334 --> 00:25:04.586
That's weird. Let me...

00:25:05.713 --> 00:25:07.965
Ah, honey? Are you still there?

00:25:08.048 --> 00:25:10.342
[man] <i>Uh, yeah. Hello?</i>

00:25:10.426 --> 00:25:11.552
Who's this?

00:25:11.635 --> 00:25:14.013
<i>This is Marvin.</i>
<i>I'm a cousin of the groom.</i>

00:25:14.096 --> 00:25:16.640
You said to call
if there was any problems.

00:25:19.268 --> 00:25:22.438
Yeah, it's pretty much since we got here.
Now it's worse.

00:25:22.521 --> 00:25:24.106
We get it fixed very soon.

00:25:24.189 --> 00:25:26.025
Oh, why not now, pal?

00:25:26.108 --> 00:25:31.613
There is some work being done
in Executive Suite directly above.

00:25:31.697 --> 00:25:33.449
-That's my dad's room?
-Yes.

00:25:34.825 --> 00:25:38.787
It's possibly possible
this work may have caused the leak.

00:25:39.997 --> 00:25:41.540
The cutting into the ceiling.

00:25:41.623 --> 00:25:43.834
Yeah, well, I'm not aware of this work.

00:25:43.917 --> 00:25:47.504
But maybe if you guys used
the inch-and-a-half copper pipes,

00:25:47.588 --> 00:25:50.799
like we suggested four years ago,
we wouldn't be in this jam right now.

00:25:50.883 --> 00:25:52.926
Can't we just get another room
in the meantime?

00:25:53.010 --> 00:25:54.219
[chuckling]

00:25:54.303 --> 00:25:57.473
Why the giggling?
Is the rest of the place booked?

00:25:57.556 --> 00:26:00.100
Well, I know there's
a Ronnie the Limo Driver book signing

00:26:00.184 --> 00:26:02.186
tomorrow in the lobby,
so the place is buzzing.

00:26:02.269 --> 00:26:03.979
That's interesting.

00:26:04.063 --> 00:26:09.026
So, uh... I can apologize to you for this.
I really am truly embarrassed.

00:26:09.109 --> 00:26:13.697
But maybe I can call some other hotels,
check on their availability.

00:26:13.781 --> 00:26:18.494
Or if we need to, you guys could crash
at our house until it's fixed.

00:26:18.577 --> 00:26:19.578
That'll work.

00:26:21.497 --> 00:26:25.584
Okay. So, we'll do that.
Hey, don't forget your gift bags.

00:26:28.128 --> 00:26:30.422
My wife and kids
put them together for you.

00:26:33.801 --> 00:26:34.885
Snapple.

00:26:34.968 --> 00:26:38.514
All local foods.
Snapple's based on Long Island.

00:26:39.056 --> 00:26:42.142
That's from the King Kullen Supermarkets,
also Long Island.

00:26:43.685 --> 00:26:45.354
Cool. Thanks.

00:26:48.148 --> 00:26:49.149
[indistinct chatter]

00:26:49.233 --> 00:26:51.401
This is so nice, right? This is great.

00:26:51.485 --> 00:26:54.404
Everybody all cozy together in one place.
I love it.

00:26:54.488 --> 00:26:56.990
Yeah, and with Noah.

00:26:57.074 --> 00:27:00.494
-Oh, yeah.
-I think this is gonna be good for him.

00:27:00.577 --> 00:27:03.038
We just have to follow
the center's instructions.

00:27:03.122 --> 00:27:06.250
Oh, sure. What can we do for you?

00:27:06.333 --> 00:27:08.877
So, obviously, no one should drink
in front of him.

00:27:08.961 --> 00:27:12.047
Oh, okay. Sure, we can make that work.

00:27:12.131 --> 00:27:15.676
Another guest with special requirements,
that's fine.

00:27:16.468 --> 00:27:17.886
No knives near him.

00:27:17.970 --> 00:27:20.180
Oh, even in the kitchen?

00:27:20.264 --> 00:27:23.433
Well, I think they mean hide them.
Not anywhere he can get to them.

00:27:23.517 --> 00:27:25.435
-[mother] Okay.
-[Lisa] No cords.

00:27:25.519 --> 00:27:29.231
Jay? What else?
[whispering] We're talking about Noah.

00:27:30.482 --> 00:27:33.235
-Did you mention the medicine cabinet?
-Oh, yeah.

00:27:33.318 --> 00:27:37.489
You should remove any medication,
pills of any kind from your cabinets.

00:27:37.573 --> 00:27:40.742
-And triggers.
-Yes, triggers. No music.

00:27:40.826 --> 00:27:42.828
No music at all?

00:27:42.911 --> 00:27:45.789
[chuckles] I only ask
'cause we're having a wedding.

00:27:45.956 --> 00:27:49.084
Not sure. You know what?
I have the list of triggers on my iPad.

00:27:49.168 --> 00:27:50.586
Do you have a printer?

00:27:57.009 --> 00:28:00.095
Oh! Kenny, Kenny, Kenny,
let my cousin help you out with that.

00:28:00.179 --> 00:28:02.389
-He's the one sleeping on it.
-She's feeding me.

00:28:02.472 --> 00:28:04.016
No, it's fine. We're having fun.

00:28:04.099 --> 00:28:06.602
-You gotta put it in the hole, honey.
-I'm trying, Dad.

00:28:06.685 --> 00:28:09.479
I know you're trying. You're doing great,
but it's better if it's in.

00:28:09.563 --> 00:28:11.231
Hey Tyler, wanna have a catch?

00:28:11.315 --> 00:28:14.860
Hey, sorry, little man. I gotta run.
But I'll be back later on tonight. Okay?

00:28:14.943 --> 00:28:16.987
-You gotta leave already?
-Yeah, I gotta take off.

00:28:17.070 --> 00:28:21.533
-She doesn't want him to leave.
-Of course she doesn't. She loves him.

00:28:22.159 --> 00:28:23.994
Yeah, you know I gotta go study.

00:28:24.077 --> 00:28:25.746
-He has to study.
-Yeah.

00:28:26.663 --> 00:28:30.083
-When are you coming back?
-She wants to know when he's coming back.

00:28:30.167 --> 00:28:31.043
-Ah.
-Aw.

00:28:33.045 --> 00:28:34.755
Now they want privacy.

00:28:36.173 --> 00:28:37.966
Hi. I'm Sarah, by the way.

00:28:38.592 --> 00:28:40.469
Sarah. Right. Nice to meet you.

00:28:40.552 --> 00:28:43.222
I'm the groom.
Which side of the family are you on?

00:28:43.305 --> 00:28:45.974
-I've lost track.
-Me, too. Me, too. Yeah.

00:28:46.058 --> 00:28:48.227
Do you wanna go somewhere quieter?

00:28:48.310 --> 00:28:51.146
[laughing] Like Mardi Gras
or a Justin Bieber concert or something?

00:28:51.230 --> 00:28:55.776
Guess what? My dad's concerned about
the open bar. Said the deal's a rip-off.

00:28:55.859 --> 00:28:57.486
Yeah, it's all good. Whatever he wants.

00:28:57.569 --> 00:28:59.947
At this point,
I just wanna look good in the pictures.

00:29:00.030 --> 00:29:02.115
Oh! I didn't see anything!

00:29:02.824 --> 00:29:04.826
There's nothing to see, brother.
Thanks. Good luck.

00:29:04.910 --> 00:29:06.620
It must be that new love shit, huh?

00:29:06.703 --> 00:29:08.956
-What?
-Okay, time to go.

00:29:10.165 --> 00:29:12.417
Okay. Happy studying. Love you.

00:29:12.501 --> 00:29:15.128
She loves him. Like I said before.

00:29:15.212 --> 00:29:17.714
Course she does! That's her guy.

00:29:18.674 --> 00:29:20.217
-[dog barking]
-[Rose] Pinky Toe!

00:29:21.885 --> 00:29:24.554
-Oh! Oh! Okay.
-[Marvin] Sorry, man.

00:29:24.638 --> 00:29:26.139
Should we keep her outside?

00:29:26.223 --> 00:29:30.102
Oh, no, no, no, it's fine.
We'll find a way to separate them.

00:29:33.397 --> 00:29:38.402
Yeah, I'm calling to get your flight
information so I can, uh, pick you up.

00:29:38.485 --> 00:29:39.444
When are you coming?

00:29:39.528 --> 00:29:42.155
Hey, look, man.
I had to get on an earlier flight.

00:29:42.239 --> 00:29:45.284
They were forecasting
bad weather out in LA.

00:29:45.367 --> 00:29:46.451
<i>So you're here?</i>

00:29:46.535 --> 00:29:48.370
Because we can get you the room.

00:29:48.453 --> 00:29:50.914
Sorry, I can't hear shit.

00:29:50.998 --> 00:29:53.125
You got an animal shelter
going on, or what?

00:29:53.208 --> 00:29:55.961
Let me find a quiet place. Hang on.

00:29:57.296 --> 00:30:02.968
I said we could get you the room tonight,
or you could stay with us.

00:30:03.051 --> 00:30:05.512
No, no, I didn't wanna put you guys out.

00:30:05.595 --> 00:30:06.763
<i>I feel bad.</i>

00:30:06.847 --> 00:30:10.017
I shouldn't have called so late.
Did I wake you up?

00:30:10.100 --> 00:30:14.062
No, no, no, I'm up reading surgery books.

00:30:14.146 --> 00:30:16.690
[Kenny] So you're in the city.
What hotel are you at?

00:30:16.773 --> 00:30:18.317
The Mandarin.

00:30:18.400 --> 00:30:22.821
Ooh! Well, you are going to love the room
we got you here.

00:30:22.904 --> 00:30:25.157
It is spectacular.

00:30:25.240 --> 00:30:29.077
[stammering] I'll pick you up
in the morning.

00:30:29.161 --> 00:30:31.079
I can get a car service, man.

00:30:31.163 --> 00:30:34.791
No. Absolutely not.
I will see you at ten o'clock.

00:30:35.417 --> 00:30:37.044
<i>I'm sorry, just one more second.</i>

00:30:38.253 --> 00:30:41.048
[mother] <i>Hi! I heard you're just</i>
<i>reading a book.</i>

00:30:41.131 --> 00:30:43.008
<i>I hope it's okay if I ask</i>
<i>one more question.</i>

00:30:43.091 --> 00:30:44.593
<i>We were told to clear out</i>
<i>our medicine...</i>

00:30:44.676 --> 00:30:45.844
Oh, shit.

00:30:45.927 --> 00:30:47.971
<i>...for a houseguest</i>
<i>who just got out of rehab,</i>

00:30:48.055 --> 00:30:51.391
and what I'm wondering is,
does that include anti-frizz shampoo?

00:30:51.475 --> 00:30:53.435
<i>Because I saw there's alcohol</i>
<i>on the label.</i>

00:30:53.518 --> 00:30:54.728
<i>I don't wanna take any chances.</i>

00:30:54.811 --> 00:30:57.606
<i>But it's a brand-new bottle, right? </i>
<i>I mean, it smells pretty good.</i>

00:30:57.689 --> 00:30:59.566
<i>I don't want anyone drinking it over ice.</i>

00:31:01.318 --> 00:31:03.487
[Kenny] Oh, my God,
it smells good in here.

00:31:03.570 --> 00:31:06.782
All right, I'm off.
I'm off to pick up the big man.

00:31:06.865 --> 00:31:09.326
-[chuckling] He's not a big man.
-Okay.

00:31:09.409 --> 00:31:11.536
Why don't you let him get a car service?

00:31:11.620 --> 00:31:14.414
-He's the one with the money.
-Okay, Iris.

00:31:17.918 --> 00:31:20.629
Oh! Hey, guys. What's doing? Come on in.

00:31:21.421 --> 00:31:23.965
-What's that?
-Oh, breakfast is cooking.

00:31:24.049 --> 00:31:28.095
I'm sorry, I didn't get
everybody's name yesterday. You're...

00:31:28.178 --> 00:31:29.930
-Leonard.
-Leonard. That's right.

00:31:30.013 --> 00:31:31.306
-Jermaine.
-Jermaine is it.

00:31:31.390 --> 00:31:32.557
That's it. There you go.

00:31:32.641 --> 00:31:36.353
Yeah. We got the killer eggs going,
and pancakes and, uh...

00:31:36.436 --> 00:31:38.897
I was on my way to pick up Dr. C, but...

00:31:38.980 --> 00:31:43.402
Hey, uh, guys, look who's here.
It's Leonard and Jermaine.

00:31:43.485 --> 00:31:46.154
I found them outside.
This is my brother, Mark.

00:31:46.238 --> 00:31:49.908
And this is Rose, my daughter,
and Iris and my wife, Debbie.

00:31:49.991 --> 00:31:51.368
Bringing it with the home fries.

00:31:51.451 --> 00:31:53.912
What do you like, pancakes, eggs?

00:31:53.995 --> 00:31:55.664
-Uh, sure.
-[laughs]

00:31:55.747 --> 00:31:57.332
-Okay, let's go.
-There's your answer.

00:31:57.416 --> 00:32:00.085
All right. And this is Noah,
over there in the corner.

00:32:00.168 --> 00:32:02.379
That's fake crystal, by the way, Noah.

00:32:02.462 --> 00:32:04.589
And where's Sarah?
Where is the bride?

00:32:04.673 --> 00:32:07.217
She is sleeping, I'm guessing,
or stretching her shoes.

00:32:07.300 --> 00:32:09.970
Hey, Marvin, Ethridge, look who's here.

00:32:11.263 --> 00:32:12.097
Hey.

00:32:12.180 --> 00:32:14.766
"Hey"? That's all they get?
For Leonard and Jermaine?

00:32:14.850 --> 00:32:16.184
You can't give them a little more?

00:32:17.018 --> 00:32:20.230
Um, how you doing? Nice to meet you.

00:32:20.313 --> 00:32:23.275
"Nice to..."
These are your family, right?

00:32:23.358 --> 00:32:25.110
-I don't know them.
-Me, neither.

00:32:25.193 --> 00:32:26.319
Not my family.

00:32:28.363 --> 00:32:29.573
Okay.

00:32:31.867 --> 00:32:34.536
-We were just walking by...
-Yeah. I get it.

00:32:35.454 --> 00:32:38.540
Go ahead and, uh...
enjoy the breakfast anyways.

00:32:40.375 --> 00:32:41.501
My mistake.

00:32:44.796 --> 00:32:47.841
Oh, good morning.
You sleep okay in Rose's room?

00:32:47.924 --> 00:32:49.843
Yeah. It was great.

00:32:49.926 --> 00:32:51.761
I like those glasses, Iris.

00:32:51.845 --> 00:32:56.975
Mark gave me a free eye exam at his store,
and then he got me these glasses cheap.

00:32:57.058 --> 00:33:00.520
Well, you got the wholesale price.
You paid what I would pay.

00:33:00.604 --> 00:33:03.064
Well, that sounds like a nice deal.
I'm in.

00:33:03.148 --> 00:33:04.441
[Iris] Family discount.

00:33:04.524 --> 00:33:06.526
Wow, that's so nice. Thank you, Mark.

00:33:06.610 --> 00:33:08.028
Yeah. Yeah, sure.

00:33:08.111 --> 00:33:10.739
-[Jay] You hear about Mark's deal?
-That's the hookup.

00:33:10.822 --> 00:33:12.616
[Jay] It's a bargain, you guys.

00:33:12.699 --> 00:33:15.869
Wait, I'm so bad with names.
Which cousin are you again?

00:33:15.952 --> 00:33:18.455
-Uh, actually we're--
-Just roll with it.

00:33:19.247 --> 00:33:21.416
-Cousin Leonard.
-Cousin Jermaine.

00:33:21.958 --> 00:33:23.543
Welcome.

00:33:23.627 --> 00:33:24.461
Thank you.

00:33:27.130 --> 00:33:30.133
[Billy Joel's "Scenes
from an Italian Restaurant" playing]

00:33:31.218 --> 00:33:34.012
Columbus Circle.
I'm going the right way, right?

00:33:34.095 --> 00:33:35.805
Keep it going. Yep.

00:33:35.889 --> 00:33:37.641
It's a Two Diamond.

00:33:37.724 --> 00:33:40.727
I mean, nothing against the place
you were staying, but...

00:33:44.564 --> 00:33:47.484
[sportscaster 1
speaking indistinctly on radio]

00:33:47.567 --> 00:33:50.654
[sportscaster 2] <i>It's not like this team</i>
<i>hasn't hit. Because they have.</i>

00:33:50.737 --> 00:33:54.491
[woman over radio] <i>...housing market.</i>
<i>Yuki Noguchi, NPR news.</i>

00:33:54.574 --> 00:33:56.368
-Hey. There he is!
-[truck honking]

00:33:56.451 --> 00:34:00.288
I... I'd get out of the car,
but that truck driver's honking at me.

00:34:00.372 --> 00:34:03.291
-No problem.
-Sir, could you pop the trunk?

00:34:03.375 --> 00:34:06.086
-Oh, uh, this is jammed. Uh...
-[honking continues]

00:34:06.169 --> 00:34:07.712
Want me to put 'em in the back seat?

00:34:07.796 --> 00:34:10.298
-No, take the key. Take the key, please.
-Take the key. Okay.

00:34:10.382 --> 00:34:11.716
Take the key. Just pop it.

00:34:11.800 --> 00:34:14.886
-Be one sec. He's gonna, he's--
-[man] Sir, there's no keyhole back here.

00:34:14.970 --> 00:34:18.014
Okay. Let me have the key back.
Just put the stuff in the back seat.

00:34:18.098 --> 00:34:19.474
-[man] You got it.
-Thank you.

00:34:23.228 --> 00:34:25.438
Got you a Starbucks. Worth it, right?

00:34:26.439 --> 00:34:30.026
Thanks, thanks,
but I may need to stay sleepy.

00:34:30.110 --> 00:34:34.364
Oh. Okay. Stayed up all night
with the surgery books?

00:34:35.615 --> 00:34:38.535
Yeah, and the electric blinds
programmed wrong.

00:34:38.618 --> 00:34:41.079
Oh. Well, this car,

00:34:41.162 --> 00:34:43.665
ah, the seats recline all the way back
if you pull the handle.

00:34:43.748 --> 00:34:45.292
I can do it for you if you want.

00:34:45.375 --> 00:34:46.793
No, I'm... I'm good.

00:34:46.876 --> 00:34:49.212
Got seat heaters, too.

00:34:49.296 --> 00:34:52.173
Just press the button.
But it's summertime, so...

00:34:52.257 --> 00:34:54.009
Yeah, my seat... My seat's fine.

00:34:54.634 --> 00:34:59.097
Well, we should be there in 45 minutes
to an hour, thirty, so...

00:34:59.180 --> 00:35:02.517
Think about reclining it.
It's there for you if you want it.

00:35:03.184 --> 00:35:08.440
And also I would crank up the AC,
you just gimme a nod.

00:35:10.692 --> 00:35:14.154
-That was a nod. Okay.
-That was an AC nod.

00:35:14.237 --> 00:35:16.573
Oh, it was the AC nod.
I thought you were nod...

00:35:16.656 --> 00:35:18.408
All right, let's see
how the window goes,

00:35:18.491 --> 00:35:20.118
and then we'll get the AC going.

00:35:24.372 --> 00:35:28.043
How we doin' with the AC? You good still?
You don't need it, right?

00:35:28.126 --> 00:35:29.085
[stammers]

00:35:29.169 --> 00:35:31.504
I'm just talking gas-wise,
it's better off.

00:35:31.588 --> 00:35:34.257
I'm just saying, AC would be great.

00:35:34.633 --> 00:35:36.843
You say it and we... We'll turn it on.

00:35:38.511 --> 00:35:39.554
I said it.

00:35:40.221 --> 00:35:43.058
That's right. 100%.

00:35:43.141 --> 00:35:46.811
I'll just hit the switch
and it's blasting.

00:35:49.439 --> 00:35:51.232
It's really hot in here.

00:35:51.316 --> 00:35:52.651
It's getting there, right?

00:35:53.777 --> 00:35:55.195
All right, go to sleep.

00:35:56.071 --> 00:35:58.990
It's hard to sleep
'cause of all the noise...

00:35:59.074 --> 00:36:01.201
-Yeah. All right.
-...from outside.

00:36:01.951 --> 00:36:05.038
-How's this? Let me turn it on for you.
-[air conditioner whirring]

00:36:05.121 --> 00:36:06.831
-Better?
-Yeah.

00:36:06.956 --> 00:36:08.833
-Okay, let's turn it off.
-Then...

00:36:11.836 --> 00:36:13.380
This is Dr. Cortice.

00:36:13.463 --> 00:36:15.423
Yes, all ready.

00:36:15.507 --> 00:36:16.883
Uh-huh. The suite?

00:36:17.509 --> 00:36:18.718
[laughing]

00:36:18.802 --> 00:36:22.138
There he is! You almost gave me
a heart attack. Mr. Last Minute, huh?

00:36:23.014 --> 00:36:25.517
You forgot? We're supposed to have
a meeting about Saturday.

00:36:25.600 --> 00:36:27.435
This guy you married.

00:36:27.519 --> 00:36:29.354
I'm gonna bring this man up to his room.

00:36:29.437 --> 00:36:30.772
[laughing] Hi, Dr. Cortice.

00:36:30.855 --> 00:36:33.233
[Kirby] Oh, stop with the "doctor."
Just call me Kirby.

00:36:33.316 --> 00:36:35.527
Look, just don't call him "Dad"
or Kenny will plotz.

00:36:35.610 --> 00:36:38.321
-That's not true. That's not true.
-You look gorgeous.

00:36:38.405 --> 00:36:41.366
I've seen her in the dress.
You're gonna have a seizure.

00:36:41.449 --> 00:36:43.493
[chuckling] Know what?
Do what you gotta do.

00:36:43.576 --> 00:36:45.662
I'm gonna hit the room.
And I'll catch you later.

00:36:45.745 --> 00:36:49.749
-No, I'm gonna bring you to the room.
-Oh, come on, Pop. He's a big boy.

00:36:49.833 --> 00:36:51.084
Hanan, you're gonna bring him--

00:36:51.167 --> 00:36:53.336
Gotta talk down the running order.
Where's the magician?

00:36:53.420 --> 00:36:54.421
We have a magician?

00:36:54.504 --> 00:36:57.382
Yes, we do, honey.
He's great. He goes table to table.

00:36:57.465 --> 00:36:59.926
He's gonna double as the emcee, too.
He does it all.

00:37:00.009 --> 00:37:02.595
Kenny, did you ever ask Sarah
if she's good with the magician?

00:37:02.679 --> 00:37:04.681
What? Now she doesn't like magicians?

00:37:04.764 --> 00:37:08.059
-Ah, here's Kent!
-Apologies, folks. Is this the bride?

00:37:08.143 --> 00:37:10.145
-Yes.
-Ah, pleasure.

00:37:10.228 --> 00:37:11.521
[all shrieking]

00:37:11.604 --> 00:37:13.565
-I'm gonna have a heart attack!
-[laughing]

00:37:13.648 --> 00:37:15.108
You see what I mean, huh?

00:37:15.191 --> 00:37:16.651
Kent, take 'em through the night.

00:37:16.735 --> 00:37:19.362
Cocktails. I'll be going around
with the light stuff:

00:37:19.446 --> 00:37:21.322
cards, coins, foam balls. Keep it simple.

00:37:21.406 --> 00:37:24.033
Wait. Magic during the cocktails?

00:37:24.117 --> 00:37:25.994
Well, you want people to stay
interested, right?

00:37:26.077 --> 00:37:27.871
-They're gonna be bored?
-I don't know.

00:37:27.954 --> 00:37:31.124
It's a fast-moving world out there.
You got computers, cellular telephones...

00:37:31.207 --> 00:37:32.333
May I continue?

00:37:32.959 --> 00:37:33.960
Yes.

00:37:34.043 --> 00:37:36.212
Wedding, photos, reception line,

00:37:36.296 --> 00:37:38.298
"Folks, if you'll find your way
to your tables,"

00:37:38.381 --> 00:37:39.257
crowd-work,

00:37:39.340 --> 00:37:40.675
"Is this your card, madam?"

00:37:40.759 --> 00:37:44.721
Boom, cheers.
"Who's the next victim?" Laughs.

00:37:45.346 --> 00:37:48.641
"Oh, I see you've forgotten this,"
pulls card from pocket,

00:37:48.725 --> 00:37:50.143
screams,

00:37:50.226 --> 00:37:53.938
"Sir, I see you really love your queens."

00:37:54.022 --> 00:37:55.106
Big laughs.

00:37:55.190 --> 00:37:58.067
"And now for the real stars of our show,"

00:37:58.151 --> 00:37:59.903
-cue band.
-DJ.

00:37:59.986 --> 00:38:01.112
-Cue DJ.
-Yes.

00:38:01.196 --> 00:38:03.448
Introduction, bridesmaids, groomsmen.

00:38:03.531 --> 00:38:05.074
We're gonna come out in pairs.

00:38:05.158 --> 00:38:06.576
And who's this?

00:38:06.659 --> 00:38:09.329
"This" is the bride's best friend.

00:38:09.412 --> 00:38:12.957
We choreographed an entrance.
It's gonna be to "Don't Stop Believin'."

00:38:13.041 --> 00:38:15.126
-[laughing] That sounds amazing.
-Right?

00:38:15.210 --> 00:38:17.670
-[man] So obvious, you gotta love it.
-[Kent] Yes. High camp.

00:38:17.754 --> 00:38:20.465
-You know what'd be hysterical?
-I know what you're thinking, Glen.

00:38:20.757 --> 00:38:22.592
-Dry ice.
-Yes. [laughing]

00:38:22.675 --> 00:38:24.385
[all chuckling]

00:38:24.469 --> 00:38:26.095
[Glen] He knows his stuff.

00:38:34.437 --> 00:38:35.355
What the...

00:38:36.689 --> 00:38:38.483
TV, color.

00:38:40.401 --> 00:38:41.611
Refrigerator is here.

00:38:41.694 --> 00:38:43.238
Mmm-hmm.

00:38:44.781 --> 00:38:46.866
Toaster. Four slice.

00:38:52.705 --> 00:38:54.207
For exercise.

00:38:54.999 --> 00:38:56.417
Or to hang myself.

00:38:56.501 --> 00:39:00.839
Is there anything else I can get for you?

00:39:00.922 --> 00:39:03.550
You know what? I'm gonna go to bed.
Long night.

00:39:04.509 --> 00:39:06.302
[laughing]

00:39:44.173 --> 00:39:46.092
-[electricity crackles]
-[Kirby exclaims]

00:39:47.969 --> 00:39:50.597
So, all you did was just pull on the cord?

00:39:50.680 --> 00:39:53.975
I didn't pull on anything.
I didn't touch it. I breathed on it.

00:39:54.058 --> 00:39:55.310
That's interesting,

00:39:55.393 --> 00:39:59.939
because I remember when we suggested
the reinforced ceilings,

00:40:00.023 --> 00:40:01.441
you didn't wanna go for that.

00:40:01.524 --> 00:40:03.276
[laughing] No.

00:40:03.359 --> 00:40:06.821
And why does the hotel have a painting
of your grandma hanging up?

00:40:06.905 --> 00:40:10.325
Oh. That's not my grandma.
That painting came with the room.

00:40:10.408 --> 00:40:12.201
But she looks just like you.

00:40:12.285 --> 00:40:13.453
Does she?

00:40:13.536 --> 00:40:16.789
I take that as a compliment
'cause that's a very attractive woman.

00:40:16.873 --> 00:40:18.291
But it's not my grandma.

00:40:19.083 --> 00:40:21.836
So, what does Rose call you?
What are you to her?

00:40:21.920 --> 00:40:23.421
[Rose] Sister's father-in-law?

00:40:23.504 --> 00:40:25.298
That's what he is, not what you call him.

00:40:25.381 --> 00:40:28.259
-Who folded the chair?
-Oh! It was blocking the path.

00:40:28.343 --> 00:40:31.179
Well, did you know
that his hands are insured?

00:40:31.262 --> 00:40:32.764
He's very important.

00:40:32.847 --> 00:40:34.974
You don't have to move the old man for me.

00:40:35.058 --> 00:40:38.686
Oh, no, no, no. He's happy wherever he is.
Don't worry about that, pal.

00:40:38.770 --> 00:40:41.940
Dr. C needin' his own space. [scoffs]

00:40:42.023 --> 00:40:44.484
Hey, Pop. Uh...

00:40:45.360 --> 00:40:48.112
-You flew into New York yesterday?
-Yeah, it was a weather thing.

00:40:48.196 --> 00:40:50.531
A weather thing in LA?

00:40:50.615 --> 00:40:54.994
Hey, I'm here.
I took my room at the Shits Carlton.

00:40:55.078 --> 00:40:57.789
Got a chandelier to the skull,
just like I requested.

00:40:57.872 --> 00:41:01.584
So, any celebrities you've worked on?

00:41:01.668 --> 00:41:02.961
-Surgery?
-[Iris] Yes.

00:41:03.044 --> 00:41:06.297
Yeah, I can't really speak
about the ones that aren't public.

00:41:06.381 --> 00:41:07.882
But you know Rosie O'Donnell?

00:41:07.966 --> 00:41:10.843
Oh, my... Debbie! Rosie McDonald!

00:41:10.927 --> 00:41:12.971
-What? What?
-He did the heart.

00:41:13.054 --> 00:41:15.974
Was she nice? She doesn't seem happy.

00:41:16.057 --> 00:41:18.476
Well, she was asleep most of the time
I was with her.

00:41:18.559 --> 00:41:20.311
Oh! Well, you see, that's rude.

00:41:20.395 --> 00:41:22.188
Ma, he means the anesthesia.

00:41:22.271 --> 00:41:23.606
[all laughing]

00:41:23.690 --> 00:41:24.857
Of course!

00:41:26.776 --> 00:41:30.279
Are you sure you wanna be part
of this crazy family?

00:41:30.363 --> 00:41:31.197
No.

00:41:32.365 --> 00:41:36.244
Sorry, guys. Remember, the loud laughing,
it's a trigger.

00:41:43.167 --> 00:41:45.211
Are we really not gonna talk
about this now?

00:41:45.294 --> 00:41:47.755
[laughing] No, Dad,
I'm not gonna have a prenup.

00:41:47.839 --> 00:41:50.383
-She's a nice girl. But...
-[rock music playing in distance]

00:41:53.803 --> 00:41:55.096
She's a nice girl,

00:41:55.179 --> 00:41:58.182
but come on, look around,
these people are broke.

00:41:58.266 --> 00:41:59.350
[cell phone buzzes]

00:41:59.434 --> 00:42:01.144
Oh, uh, one second.

00:42:02.562 --> 00:42:04.522
-Hey, Kenny.
-[Kenny] Yeah?

00:42:04.605 --> 00:42:06.357
Kenny. Real quick.

00:42:09.193 --> 00:42:11.738
-Oh. All right! Small problem.
-Yeah?

00:42:11.821 --> 00:42:14.782
-I'll fix it. I'll shoot over.
-Okay.

00:42:14.866 --> 00:42:15.825
I'll go with ya.

00:42:15.908 --> 00:42:18.703
No, no, no! You hang out here! You relax!

00:42:18.786 --> 00:42:22.540
It definitely burns.
Yes. It's killing me.

00:42:23.166 --> 00:42:26.544
Ask him. I mean, he's not a urologist,
but I'm sure he'd take a look.

00:42:26.627 --> 00:42:28.129
I'm going with you.

00:42:28.212 --> 00:42:31.591
Okay, gotta run over to the hotel.
Be back in a few.

00:42:31.674 --> 00:42:33.009
Seymour, do you need to go?

00:42:33.634 --> 00:42:35.178
Seymour, Kenny's leaving.

00:42:35.261 --> 00:42:37.305
[Roberta] Seymour, can you wake up?

00:42:40.308 --> 00:42:41.350
Why did he--

00:42:41.434 --> 00:42:43.186
[Kirby] You need a valet
to move these cars.

00:42:43.269 --> 00:42:45.855
No, we'll take my wife's minivan.

00:42:45.938 --> 00:42:48.649
You drive with your seat
that close to the wheel?

00:42:48.733 --> 00:42:51.986
Yeah, it's good. This way I'm closer
to the button. It's...

00:42:52.070 --> 00:42:54.322
Yeah, but you go full leg
in the other car.

00:42:54.405 --> 00:42:55.823
-Yeah.
-Okay.

00:42:55.907 --> 00:42:58.076
Uh, whose room are we going to?

00:42:58.159 --> 00:43:01.996
-Uh, your daughter's room. And--
-My ex-mother-in-law.

00:43:02.080 --> 00:43:03.915
-Seymour's up!
-Come on.

00:43:04.040 --> 00:43:06.626
-Incredible. All right.
-Seymour's up!

00:43:06.709 --> 00:43:08.878
-Goodbye. Goodbye, already.
-He has to go!

00:43:08.961 --> 00:43:11.422
Hey, he has to go!

00:43:12.381 --> 00:43:15.051
So, it's... The leak's just spreading now.

00:43:15.843 --> 00:43:20.556
This is because of the doctor's suite
the workers had to fix. [chuckling]

00:43:20.640 --> 00:43:23.309
-Okay.
-Oh! It's all about the doctor now?

00:43:23.392 --> 00:43:26.312
Same doctor that found the tumor
on your CAT scan.

00:43:26.395 --> 00:43:28.773
Stage two. Big-ass deal.

00:43:28.856 --> 00:43:31.400
Beat it, dunked on it, moved on.

00:43:32.151 --> 00:43:34.112
Uh, and the hotel's completely booked?

00:43:34.195 --> 00:43:35.947
[laughing] It is squishy.

00:43:36.030 --> 00:43:39.534
Oh, yeah! You heard the squishy noise.
And it made you laugh more.

00:43:39.617 --> 00:43:41.327
You know, I can get you guys a lifeguard

00:43:41.410 --> 00:43:43.579
or move you into a nicer place
till they fix this.

00:43:43.663 --> 00:43:44.664
[both] No!

00:43:44.747 --> 00:43:46.582
We don't need your nice place, Dad.

00:43:46.666 --> 00:43:50.044
I'm not gonna be separated
from the family. <i>I </i>value family.

00:43:50.128 --> 00:43:51.087
Okay, okay.

00:43:52.171 --> 00:43:53.381
I hear the squish.

00:43:53.464 --> 00:43:56.217
There's plenty of families staying
at our house, including your father.

00:43:56.300 --> 00:43:57.468
You're welcome to join us.

00:43:57.552 --> 00:43:59.428
Thank you. That sounds fine.

00:43:59.512 --> 00:44:04.517
These sweaters I'd laid out got leaked on.
I expect to be compensated.

00:44:04.600 --> 00:44:06.686
Oh. We'll work on that. Ah...

00:44:06.769 --> 00:44:09.397
Until then, there's something else
I can do for you ladies.

00:44:09.480 --> 00:44:11.649
[Billy Joel's "Modern Woman" playing]

00:44:11.732 --> 00:44:16.279
<i>♪ She understands</i>
<i>The things you're doing ♪</i>

00:44:16.362 --> 00:44:21.367
<i>♪ She's a modern woman ♪</i>

00:44:22.034 --> 00:44:23.536
[Marvin] Parcheesi?

00:44:23.619 --> 00:44:25.204
[grandmother] Never heard of
Parcheesi?

00:44:25.288 --> 00:44:26.873
[Debbie] It's more fun than it looks!

00:44:26.956 --> 00:44:30.918
It's from an old Indian game.
The Parcheesi tribe, I think.

00:44:31.002 --> 00:44:32.670
Is that right, Ma?
I never heard that one.

00:44:32.753 --> 00:44:34.422
'Cause that's not true. At all.

00:44:34.505 --> 00:44:36.632
[Roberta] Okay, Mr. Know-It-All.
Look it up.

00:44:36.716 --> 00:44:38.634
He won't look it up, 'cause you're right.

00:44:38.718 --> 00:44:40.553
[all laughing]

00:44:40.636 --> 00:44:42.805
Dad, where do we put these?

00:44:42.889 --> 00:44:44.849
Wait a minute. Everyone, look at this.

00:44:44.932 --> 00:44:46.976
My kids are helping for the first time.

00:44:47.059 --> 00:44:49.896
-Oh, stop it.
-Congratulations.

00:44:49.979 --> 00:44:52.732
Take it to the office,
where Dr. Cortice was gonna sleep.

00:44:52.815 --> 00:44:54.150
Okay, yeah. You take those there.

00:44:54.233 --> 00:44:56.152
-Is that where we're gonna be tonight?
-Yeah.

00:44:56.235 --> 00:44:58.821
Dr. Cortice, you can take our bedroom.
I never sleep anyway.

00:44:58.905 --> 00:45:02.241
No, she'll vacuum all night long.
You'll hear that.

00:45:02.325 --> 00:45:04.410
-Hey, how come--
-[Debbie] It's my guilty pleasure.

00:45:04.493 --> 00:45:06.078
How come nobody sleeps down here, though?

00:45:06.162 --> 00:45:09.415
It's nice, the game room, right?
It's just the asbestos.

00:45:09.498 --> 00:45:11.667
It's fine for a couple of hours,
but not a whole night.

00:45:12.418 --> 00:45:14.170
-What?
-No, it's good in moderation.

00:45:14.253 --> 00:45:15.880
In moderation, it's fine.

00:45:15.963 --> 00:45:19.258
Okay, so, Kelly and me were thinking,
"What has never been done before?"

00:45:19.342 --> 00:45:21.219
And then it hits us, boom.

00:45:21.302 --> 00:45:24.305
We come out and do
a whole evolution of dance thing.

00:45:24.388 --> 00:45:26.098
Right, like, we start with the disco

00:45:26.182 --> 00:45:29.560
and then we go all the way to the Whip
and the Nae Nae.

00:45:29.644 --> 00:45:32.104
Isn't this supposed to be,
like, 20 seconds?

00:45:32.188 --> 00:45:35.066
Okay, please don't be jealous,
this is Sarah's time.

00:45:35.149 --> 00:45:38.236
So, we come out
in our John Travolta jackets and...

00:45:38.319 --> 00:45:40.404
[groaning dramatically]

00:45:42.114 --> 00:45:43.407
What happened to your face?

00:45:43.491 --> 00:45:45.201
Oh, my God, is that an allergy?

00:45:46.410 --> 00:45:47.453
What're you doing?

00:45:48.246 --> 00:45:50.206
Ah, I'm coming over.

00:45:50.289 --> 00:45:53.709
Me and Iris have to finish our game
of gin rummy. We're tied.

00:45:54.502 --> 00:45:55.795
Fun.

00:45:55.878 --> 00:45:59.674
Well, we were just about to hit up
the Noodle Bar in Syosset,

00:45:59.757 --> 00:46:03.386
sit outside the bathroom and rate the guys
as they come out. [laughing]

00:46:03.469 --> 00:46:06.180
Or I saw online,
there's this stretching class.

00:46:06.264 --> 00:46:08.307
-Oh, yes!
-So, Sarah needs to decompress

00:46:08.391 --> 00:46:10.226
and it is RumChata shot night, okay?

00:46:10.309 --> 00:46:12.270
Get the bags.
Is this your going-out clothes?

00:46:12.353 --> 00:46:13.479
I only have three shirts.

00:46:13.562 --> 00:46:15.940
-[Emily] I like that one.
-[Danielle] Yeah, thank you.

00:46:16.023 --> 00:46:18.943
-Nine, ten, eleven, twelve!
-[exclaims]

00:46:19.026 --> 00:46:20.111
[all exclaiming]

00:46:20.987 --> 00:46:22.571
[Kirby] You have another move.

00:46:22.655 --> 00:46:24.115
-Fourteen.
-What now?

00:46:24.198 --> 00:46:28.286
Well, it says in the rules,
if you roll a doublet,

00:46:28.369 --> 00:46:31.205
you get to move
what's on the other side of the dice.

00:46:31.289 --> 00:46:33.874
-A doublet?
-I never played that way. Opposites?

00:46:33.958 --> 00:46:36.502
We're good. Thanks anyway, Doublet.

00:46:36.585 --> 00:46:37.545
Doublet.

00:46:37.628 --> 00:46:39.130
[snickering] Doublet.

00:46:39.213 --> 00:46:42.258
[Ethridge] Morgan!
Get to business, Morgan! Come on!

00:46:49.223 --> 00:46:50.057
[line ringing]

00:46:50.141 --> 00:46:51.142
[cell phone ringing]

00:46:52.435 --> 00:46:54.562
-Hello?
-Hey, what's up, girl?

00:46:55.313 --> 00:46:57.982
"Girl"? What do you want, Kirby?

00:46:58.065 --> 00:47:02.528
Well, you know, I figured
since we're in the same city and all,

00:47:02.611 --> 00:47:03.738
maybe I could come over and--

00:47:03.821 --> 00:47:06.574
We're in the same city all the time. LA.

00:47:06.657 --> 00:47:10.202
Yeah, but our baby's getting married.

00:47:10.286 --> 00:47:12.997
<i>You know? That baby we made together?</i>

00:47:13.080 --> 00:47:14.040
Mmm-mmm.

00:47:14.123 --> 00:47:17.835
I'm here with Ignacio.
I'll see you at the rehearsal dinner.

00:47:17.918 --> 00:47:21.088
Well, you know, I just thought maybe
you might wanna hang out

00:47:21.172 --> 00:47:23.424
with a grown-up for a change.
That's all.

00:47:23.507 --> 00:47:25.509
Are you really trying to booty call me

00:47:25.593 --> 00:47:28.512
just so that you could get out of
that house with all your relatives?

00:47:29.096 --> 00:47:31.015
Booty call? Why would you even go there?

00:47:31.098 --> 00:47:34.060
You think I don't talk
to my mother? Doublet.

00:47:34.143 --> 00:47:38.647
Doublet? That's the rules!
Those are the actual rules of the game!

00:47:38.731 --> 00:47:43.110
I got all the grown-up I need
right here.

00:47:43.194 --> 00:47:44.779
-Thank you.
-[chuckling]

00:47:46.655 --> 00:47:47.698
What's up, man?

00:47:48.449 --> 00:47:51.619
-I'm all right.
-[sighs] Fucking Lakers.

00:47:52.203 --> 00:47:53.037
Yeah.

00:47:55.039 --> 00:47:57.541
Uh-huh. We'll see you Friday.

00:48:12.390 --> 00:48:14.683
[Noah muttering] I'm in control,
I'm in control.

00:48:14.767 --> 00:48:17.353
I'm a good person. I'm a good person.
I have dreams.

00:48:17.436 --> 00:48:18.562
I have aspirations.

00:48:18.646 --> 00:48:22.858
I have things that are going on in my head
whether anyone believes it or not. Okay?

00:48:22.942 --> 00:48:24.276
You don't know me.

00:48:26.612 --> 00:48:27.613
So, what's up?

00:48:29.115 --> 00:48:30.574
Don't pretend you wanna talk.

00:48:34.245 --> 00:48:35.996
You can write prescriptions, right?

00:48:36.997 --> 00:48:39.875
I am not going to jail for you.

00:48:40.501 --> 00:48:43.045
Look, I don't wanna freak you out.

00:48:43.129 --> 00:48:46.757
But there is a significant chance
that I will burn this house down

00:48:46.841 --> 00:48:49.301
if I'm not on drugs
within the next two hours.

00:48:49.385 --> 00:48:52.221
Oh, if my ex-wife is in here
when you burn it down,

00:48:52.304 --> 00:48:54.140
I'll give you all the pills you want.

00:48:54.640 --> 00:48:56.016
[sighing]

00:49:02.898 --> 00:49:04.150
[snoring]

00:49:10.322 --> 00:49:11.449
[snoring]

00:49:14.702 --> 00:49:15.995
[snoring]

00:49:17.371 --> 00:49:18.747
[Kirby grunting]

00:49:18.831 --> 00:49:20.583
Ah, so sexy.

00:49:21.167 --> 00:49:23.335
Work it. Uh-huh!

00:49:25.129 --> 00:49:28.132
Damn. Look at those!

00:49:31.177 --> 00:49:33.095
[grunting] Whoo!

00:49:34.013 --> 00:49:38.100
Feel good. These are firm, girl!

00:49:38.893 --> 00:49:41.520
I wonder if they taste
as good as they feel.

00:49:42.563 --> 00:49:44.857
Ah, yeah. Ah, yeah.

00:49:46.025 --> 00:49:47.693
Ooh, I'ma get all up in there.

00:49:49.236 --> 00:49:51.155
[exclaims, shouts]

00:49:53.491 --> 00:49:55.659
[grunts, grumbles]

00:49:55.743 --> 00:49:57.161
-[shouting continues]
-What?

00:49:57.244 --> 00:49:58.704
-Is there a burglar?
-No!

00:49:58.787 --> 00:50:00.080
I got the bat! Take this.

00:50:00.164 --> 00:50:01.248
[screams]

00:50:01.332 --> 00:50:04.627
-My hands! My hands!
-Are these the ones that are insured?

00:50:04.710 --> 00:50:08.130
Yeah! They're my hands!
Oh! Oh! Oh!

00:50:08.214 --> 00:50:09.882
-What the shit?
-[Debbie] There you go!

00:50:09.965 --> 00:50:12.384
It's honey. It's the best thing
to soothe the pain.

00:50:12.468 --> 00:50:15.429
There you go.
Just leave that on for ten minutes.

00:50:15.513 --> 00:50:16.764
Ah! Ah!

00:50:16.847 --> 00:50:17.973
-[screams]
-[barks]

00:50:18.057 --> 00:50:19.016
[thuds]

00:50:19.099 --> 00:50:21.101
[dog licking]

00:50:22.853 --> 00:50:25.689
[speaking Spanish]

00:50:35.032 --> 00:50:37.993
Are you here yet? He's outta clothes.

00:50:38.077 --> 00:50:40.287
Well, I didn't want him to overpack.

00:50:40.371 --> 00:50:41.914
[man] <i>You can't wash what he has?</i>

00:50:41.997 --> 00:50:44.500
Charles, we have a wedding
this week! It's--

00:50:44.583 --> 00:50:48.087
All he's got left
is his old, moldy army uniform.

00:50:48.170 --> 00:50:51.048
Well, it fits him again
since the diabetes.

00:50:51.131 --> 00:50:52.550
[chuckles] He likes it.

00:50:52.633 --> 00:50:57.846
Wasn't he, like, discharged for skipping
boot camp during Passover or something?

00:50:57.930 --> 00:51:02.601
Hey, he served his time. He did, like,
11 months in Texas or somewhere.

00:51:03.102 --> 00:51:06.647
Anyway, you're getting him a tux, no?
He doesn't have a tux.

00:51:06.730 --> 00:51:07.982
You understand that, right?

00:51:08.065 --> 00:51:09.066
Yes, yes.

00:51:09.149 --> 00:51:12.820
Just come here, please, and get the booze
like you said you would.

00:51:12.903 --> 00:51:15.197
Don't worry. I'm getting a deal, here.

00:51:15.281 --> 00:51:17.658
Haitian guy I met on the plane
is setting me up.

00:51:17.741 --> 00:51:18.909
[Kenny] <i>Great. Thank you.</i>

00:51:18.993 --> 00:51:21.829
<i>Yes, you got the arm.</i>
<i>Right there, Seymour.</i>

00:51:21.912 --> 00:51:23.706
You okay, Seymour?

00:51:24.290 --> 00:51:26.625
-[Seymour] Brake. Brake.
-Brake?

00:51:26.709 --> 00:51:29.169
[Kenny] Brake. Brake. Yeah.

00:51:29.253 --> 00:51:30.963
[indistinct chatter]

00:51:32.590 --> 00:51:35.259
Dominic, Lazzero,
I'm gonna need another tux.

00:51:35.342 --> 00:51:38.554
I didn't realize my uncle Seymour
doesn't have one.

00:51:38.637 --> 00:51:40.389
Wow, look at this man.

00:51:40.472 --> 00:51:43.267
-Thank you for your service.
-[Seymour] It's okay.

00:51:43.350 --> 00:51:45.644
You kidding me? You didn't tell me, Kenny.

00:51:45.728 --> 00:51:47.354
What? No, no, he's not--

00:51:47.438 --> 00:51:50.232
We're gonna take good care of you.
You're not gonna spend a dime.

00:51:50.316 --> 00:51:52.610
We don't get heroes here very much.

00:51:52.693 --> 00:51:53.694
World War II, right?

00:51:53.777 --> 00:51:55.946
-Yep.
-No one here's paying.

00:51:56.030 --> 00:51:58.949
I got your whole family, Seymour.
Bless you.

00:51:59.533 --> 00:52:01.827
[Lazzero] Greatest goddamn
generation right over here.

00:52:01.910 --> 00:52:04.747
You got that right.
Freakin' legs blown off.

00:52:06.498 --> 00:52:09.918
Did he just say nobody's paying
for anything?

00:52:10.002 --> 00:52:12.379
Yeah, what'd you say to them?

00:52:12.463 --> 00:52:15.215
I didn't lie. He was in World War II.

00:52:15.799 --> 00:52:17.551
Here you go, Uncle Seymour.

00:52:17.635 --> 00:52:20.012
I got arms. Just hand me the chicken.

00:52:20.095 --> 00:52:21.555
I wanna say this.

00:52:21.639 --> 00:52:24.642
Last week, we had
Ronnie the Limo Driver in here.

00:52:24.725 --> 00:52:27.311
This is bigger. This means more.

00:52:29.396 --> 00:52:31.357
Ah! Look at this guy. Huh?

00:52:31.940 --> 00:52:33.192
Lookin' sharp, kiddo.

00:52:33.275 --> 00:52:34.109
Dad?

00:52:34.860 --> 00:52:37.696
How do you like it, Isaac? Is it okay?

00:52:38.197 --> 00:52:39.490
Is it itchy?

00:52:39.573 --> 00:52:42.284
Don't worry. If it's itchy,
we'll find you another one.

00:52:42.368 --> 00:52:44.828
-[Lazzero] That's a nice tux.
-But the kid isn't happy.

00:52:44.912 --> 00:52:45.746
[Isaac sniffles]

00:52:45.829 --> 00:52:49.166
You are happy? No? Why are you upset?

00:52:50.292 --> 00:52:52.920
Isaac, come on. We don't got time.
We gotta move...

00:52:53.003 --> 00:52:55.964
The game! Oh, shit! Sorry!

00:52:56.048 --> 00:52:57.508
Guys, guys, we gotta go!

00:52:57.591 --> 00:52:59.426
The kid's got a game.

00:52:59.510 --> 00:53:01.095
We're gonna watch you, Isaac.

00:53:01.178 --> 00:53:02.846
We're all gonna watch Isaac.

00:53:02.930 --> 00:53:04.765
[crowd clapping]

00:53:08.102 --> 00:53:09.978
[man 1] Isaac, go big!

00:53:10.062 --> 00:53:11.271
[man 2] Let's go, Isaac!

00:53:11.355 --> 00:53:13.524
[Kenny] How do you not know
where the field is, Ma?

00:53:13.607 --> 00:53:16.151
You've been coming for six years already.

00:53:16.235 --> 00:53:18.987
Just turn on the GPS, then.

00:53:19.071 --> 00:53:21.907
What do you mean,
the lady's voice frightens you?

00:53:21.990 --> 00:53:23.951
Turn the volume down, then.

00:53:24.034 --> 00:53:26.870
I don't know what to tell you, Ma.
This is...

00:53:26.954 --> 00:53:29.748
-[crowd cheering and clapping]
-I can't hear you.

00:53:30.999 --> 00:53:32.584
Stay calm, Ma.

00:53:33.168 --> 00:53:35.421
What? Oh, yeah. Oh, yeah.

00:53:35.504 --> 00:53:39.007
-Thank you for your service.
-What a hero. World War II, right?

00:53:39.091 --> 00:53:40.509
Yep.

00:53:40.592 --> 00:53:41.969
What do you say, Eva?

00:53:42.052 --> 00:53:44.430
-Thanks for killing the Nazis.
-Good girl.

00:53:45.013 --> 00:53:46.849
Yeah, yeah. Thank--

00:53:48.767 --> 00:53:51.520
-Him? Yeah, yeah, sure.
-[man] A real hero!

00:53:52.771 --> 00:53:55.232
They do know his legs
are from diabetes, right?

00:53:55.315 --> 00:53:59.236
-Ah... Never came up.
-[male announcer] <i>Ladies and gentlemen,</i>

00:53:59.319 --> 00:54:04.158
<i>to throw out the first pitch,</i>
<i>World War II veteran, Seymour Lustig.</i>

00:54:04.241 --> 00:54:06.034
[crowd cheering and clapping]

00:54:06.618 --> 00:54:09.329
He was in World War II. In Texas.

00:54:09.413 --> 00:54:10.831
[man] Our hero!

00:54:15.169 --> 00:54:16.545
[crowd cheers]

00:54:16.628 --> 00:54:18.297
[bugle music playing on speaker]

00:54:21.300 --> 00:54:22.718
All right, let's go.

00:54:22.801 --> 00:54:25.262
Everybody's a winner!
Everybody's a winner!

00:54:25.846 --> 00:54:27.765
Every day's the World Series.

00:54:29.975 --> 00:54:33.395
-Where's Isaac?
-I guess he's not starting.

00:54:33.479 --> 00:54:34.354
Boo!

00:54:34.438 --> 00:54:35.939
[all] Boo!

00:54:36.023 --> 00:54:37.608
[booing continues]

00:54:39.276 --> 00:54:41.737
He'll get in the game, guys!

00:54:41.820 --> 00:54:44.448
-Put Isaac in!
-That's gobbledygook!

00:54:50.078 --> 00:54:51.914
[woman] Run, Bobby! Run!

00:54:52.539 --> 00:54:53.499
[all gasp]

00:54:53.582 --> 00:54:54.500
[Noah] You suck!

00:54:54.583 --> 00:54:55.834
Put Isaac in!

00:54:55.918 --> 00:54:57.669
Okay, you can't--

00:54:57.753 --> 00:55:00.172
Please don't discourage Noah.
He needs the release.

00:55:00.255 --> 00:55:02.800
-Get that shitty kid out of there!
-Yeah!

00:55:02.883 --> 00:55:04.885
{\an8}Send that little bitch home!

00:55:04.968 --> 00:55:07.638
{\an8}Isaac! Isaac!

00:55:07.721 --> 00:55:10.349
{\an8}[all chanting] Isaac! Isaac!

00:55:10.432 --> 00:55:12.309
-Isaac! Issac!
-Who's Isaac?

00:55:12.392 --> 00:55:14.561
I think it's the war hero's grandkid.

00:55:14.645 --> 00:55:17.439
Oh. Isaac! Isaac!

00:55:17.523 --> 00:55:19.149
Isaac!

00:55:19.233 --> 00:55:21.109
Isaac! Isaac!

00:55:21.193 --> 00:55:23.695
Isaac! Isaac! Isaac!

00:55:24.488 --> 00:55:29.076
All right, Isaac, you're gonna bat for Max
when he comes up next inning.

00:55:30.118 --> 00:55:31.662
Your name's Isaac?

00:55:37.417 --> 00:55:39.878
[all] Isaac! Isaac!

00:55:39.962 --> 00:55:41.004
[all cheer]

00:55:48.178 --> 00:55:52.724
[Kenny] He's upset. He's upset.
He's upset. He's upset.

00:55:53.350 --> 00:55:54.184
Okay.

00:55:55.060 --> 00:55:56.728
Listen, it's just a game, Isaac.

00:55:56.812 --> 00:55:58.355
Don't worry about it.

00:55:59.982 --> 00:56:02.651
Whatever happens, everyone loves you.

00:56:04.820 --> 00:56:07.114
-[umpire] Strike one.
-[crowd] Boo!

00:56:07.781 --> 00:56:10.242
That was low!
Are you outta your mind, Eddie?

00:56:10.325 --> 00:56:13.120
Thanks for the wedding invite, Ken.
I've only known you 15 years.

00:56:13.203 --> 00:56:15.998
Are you kidding me? Am I supposed to
invite the whole town?

00:56:18.542 --> 00:56:19.585
[Eddie] Strike two.

00:56:19.668 --> 00:56:21.169
[crowd booing and clamoring]

00:56:22.671 --> 00:56:24.840
That's all right.
Keep your eye on the ball.

00:56:24.923 --> 00:56:26.341
Just make contact, buddy.

00:56:26.425 --> 00:56:27.384
Just make contact.

00:56:27.467 --> 00:56:30.470
We'll get ice cream after
no matter what, okay?

00:56:32.931 --> 00:56:33.849
[crowd cheers]

00:56:33.932 --> 00:56:35.058
Go! Go!

00:56:35.142 --> 00:56:37.394
-[player] I got it! I got it!
-[grunts]

00:56:37.477 --> 00:56:39.104
[cheering]

00:56:43.275 --> 00:56:44.276
Yes!

00:56:45.444 --> 00:56:47.362
Yeah! Yeah, buddy, yeah!

00:56:48.196 --> 00:56:49.197
Matt, you okay?

00:56:50.073 --> 00:56:51.617
Hang on a second, buddy.

00:56:51.700 --> 00:56:53.702
[crowd] Isaac! Isaac!

00:56:53.785 --> 00:56:55.579
Thank you for your service.

00:56:55.662 --> 00:56:57.205
Isaac! Isaac!

00:56:57.289 --> 00:56:58.957
Isaac! Isaac!

00:56:59.041 --> 00:57:02.169
Isaac! Issac! Issac!

00:57:02.252 --> 00:57:04.880
Isaac! Isaac! Isaac!

00:57:04.963 --> 00:57:07.716
Isaac! Isaac! Isaac!

00:57:07.799 --> 00:57:09.551
[Charles] Damn!
I missed the game, huh?

00:57:09.635 --> 00:57:11.470
I heard a kid got hurt.

00:57:12.054 --> 00:57:13.931
-[Seymour] Charles?
-Hey, Pops, don't get up.

00:57:14.014 --> 00:57:15.766
[chuckles] He loves those jokes.

00:57:16.350 --> 00:57:19.061
Hey, glad you got here.
What's with the bags?

00:57:19.645 --> 00:57:22.648
It's the booze for the wedding.
All duty-free, baby.

00:57:23.565 --> 00:57:25.609
What is that? Chivas?

00:57:25.692 --> 00:57:28.195
Yeah, and not a dime in taxes.

00:57:28.278 --> 00:57:30.197
They say this should feed about 200.

00:57:30.781 --> 00:57:33.575
{\an8}I'm sorry. I know you're doing
everything you can, and I love you, but--

00:57:33.659 --> 00:57:35.994
Mr. Lustig, I can't let this happen.

00:57:36.745 --> 00:57:38.205
What the...

00:57:38.288 --> 00:57:39.539
Why is that one open?

00:57:39.623 --> 00:57:41.792
Come on, it was a two-hour Uber ride
from the airport.

00:57:43.377 --> 00:57:44.419
[Charles grunts]

00:57:46.046 --> 00:57:47.673
In case anybody wants some smokes.

00:57:48.256 --> 00:57:49.591
And...

00:57:50.425 --> 00:57:52.594
this bad boy is gonna light up
the dessert table.

00:57:53.178 --> 00:57:54.179
You ate some.

00:57:54.763 --> 00:57:57.933
I ate, like, one-fiftieth.
Geez. You're welcome.

00:57:58.016 --> 00:58:00.394
-[Sarah] Dad!
-Listen...

00:58:00.769 --> 00:58:04.022
I will speak to the caterer.
We'll figure it out right away.

00:58:04.106 --> 00:58:05.107
I promise you.

00:58:05.691 --> 00:58:07.818
See, this is what happens
when you try to cut corners.

00:58:07.901 --> 00:58:09.861
You can't have bottles like this.

00:58:09.987 --> 00:58:12.280
That's cheesy. Extra cheese, man.

00:58:12.364 --> 00:58:13.240
Okay.

00:58:13.323 --> 00:58:14.366
-Dear.
-Yes.

00:58:14.449 --> 00:58:17.911
We don't mind pitching in
for some regular bottles. Honestly.

00:58:17.995 --> 00:58:19.621
No, no. No, Mom, it's okay.

00:58:19.705 --> 00:58:24.001
Mr. Lustig just wanted to make sure
there was enough booze for Robin, so...

00:58:24.084 --> 00:58:27.671
Look, I can get you decanters so you
don't have to look at these bottles.

00:58:27.754 --> 00:58:29.506
That's actually a smart idea.

00:58:29.589 --> 00:58:31.341
I mean, it's up to you guys, but...

00:58:32.467 --> 00:58:34.511
-Okay, that could work.
-[Kenny] Yeah?

00:58:34.594 --> 00:58:36.722
I mean... That's wonderful. I...

00:58:36.805 --> 00:58:38.265
-We should get ready.
-Kenny!

00:58:38.348 --> 00:58:39.850
-We got parties--
-Why's your hair wet?

00:58:39.933 --> 00:58:41.685
-My hair's wet?
-Yeah. Why's it all wet?

00:58:42.352 --> 00:58:43.687
What the hell is...

00:58:45.856 --> 00:58:48.734
-Why is this happening, pal?
-This room priority, yes?

00:58:48.817 --> 00:58:53.113
I know. I know. But why's the rest
of the hotel going to shit?

00:58:53.196 --> 00:58:54.322
[worker] Sir?

00:58:54.406 --> 00:58:57.284
They were supposed to shut off
the water to the whole line of rooms,

00:58:57.367 --> 00:58:58.493
and didn't until now.

00:58:58.577 --> 00:59:02.289
Oh, okay. Why would somebody
forget to do that?

00:59:02.372 --> 00:59:03.623
[laughing]

00:59:03.707 --> 00:59:05.751
[shouting] What the hell is so funny?

00:59:06.251 --> 00:59:08.712
Nobody else is laughing.

00:59:08.795 --> 00:59:10.756
Why are you laughing?

00:59:10.839 --> 00:59:12.215
These sheets!

00:59:12.299 --> 00:59:14.926
[Kirby] The honey! The stupid honey!

00:59:15.010 --> 00:59:16.762
-[Kenny] How'd you sleep?
-[Kirby] Like...

00:59:16.845 --> 00:59:21.141
This damn honey's everywhere, man!
I'm trying to get this honey off!

00:59:21.224 --> 00:59:24.144
-You look good, buddy.
-[Hanan continues laughing]

00:59:25.437 --> 00:59:26.730
How come I got no water?

00:59:26.813 --> 00:59:28.315
Turn the water on. Turn--

00:59:28.398 --> 00:59:30.692
-But if water--
-[Kirby] I need water to wash this...

00:59:30.776 --> 00:59:31.860
Turn the water on!

00:59:31.943 --> 00:59:33.987
-[Kenny] Turn it on!
-...off my werewolf hands!

00:59:34.071 --> 00:59:35.447
-Go. On.
-[Kirby] Water! Help!

00:59:35.530 --> 00:59:37.949
Somebody help me! Please!

00:59:38.033 --> 00:59:39.201
[screams]

00:59:39.284 --> 00:59:40.911
-It's boiling!
-Cold water.

00:59:40.994 --> 00:59:42.913
-[Kirby] It's boiling hot!
-Cold water too.

00:59:42.996 --> 00:59:45.207
[Kirby] What're you people
trying to do to my hands?

00:59:45.290 --> 00:59:47.751
Ah... Oh, thank you.

00:59:47.834 --> 00:59:49.294
-Okay.
-[Kirby] Praise God!

00:59:49.377 --> 00:59:51.797
-[Kenny] What're you doing?
-[Kirby] What's going on?

00:59:52.339 --> 00:59:54.549
-[Kenny] Turn the water back on!
-[Kirby] Why's it off?

00:59:55.133 --> 00:59:57.010
What? What now?

00:59:57.094 --> 01:00:00.597
-The water...
-It can only be on a minute, or...

01:00:00.680 --> 01:00:02.182
Or? Or what?

01:00:08.730 --> 01:00:09.815
You know what?

01:00:09.898 --> 01:00:11.858
That's it. We did your thing.

01:00:11.942 --> 01:00:13.777
Your 99-cent wedding,

01:00:13.860 --> 01:00:17.656
and the booze bottles for giants,
and the spoonin' with Uncle Stumpy.

01:00:17.739 --> 01:00:20.700
Let me bail us outta this, okay?

01:00:20.784 --> 01:00:24.121
I'm gonna get my assistant.
She's gonna make some calls.

01:00:24.204 --> 01:00:27.666
And we're gonna move the wedding
to Manhattan.

01:00:27.749 --> 01:00:30.836
You don't have to, pal. We're all set.
I can make this work.

01:00:30.919 --> 01:00:33.755
Buddy. Pal. It's not a competition.

01:00:33.839 --> 01:00:35.966
-You don't have to feel bad.
-I don't.

01:00:36.049 --> 01:00:39.427
I don't feel bad
because I know I can fix it.

01:00:39.511 --> 01:00:40.428
[Kirby sighs]

01:00:41.346 --> 01:00:42.305
[chuckles softly]

01:00:43.515 --> 01:00:44.599
Listen.

01:00:45.225 --> 01:00:49.896
Every father looks forward
to making a wedding for their girl.

01:00:49.980 --> 01:00:51.106
You understand?

01:00:51.690 --> 01:00:55.527
I have been able to help my kids
their entire lives.

01:00:55.610 --> 01:00:57.654
I'll be able to figure this one out.

01:00:58.363 --> 01:01:04.870
Honey, maybe the thing to figure out is
to let Kirby pay for the wedding.

01:01:05.370 --> 01:01:07.080
Some of it?

01:01:07.164 --> 01:01:08.248
[chuckles]

01:01:08.331 --> 01:01:09.708
[Kenny] Maybe we don't have money

01:01:09.791 --> 01:01:12.627
because you spend it all
on the Home Shopping crap!

01:01:12.711 --> 01:01:15.505
[Debbie] That bottle keeps my coffee hot
for 12 hours!

01:01:15.589 --> 01:01:19.259
-[Kenny] What do you save coffee for?
-[Debbie] I'm not a wasteful person!

01:01:19.342 --> 01:01:22.220
-Are they gonna get a divorce?
-They never do.

01:01:22.304 --> 01:01:24.014
