01:14:15.117 --> 01:14:16.619
I've been alone with him for years.

01:14:16.702 --> 01:14:20.665
Yes, but you might wanna
share with him right now.

01:14:20.915 --> 01:14:22.500
It's healthy for both of you.

01:14:23.000 --> 01:14:24.293
Closure.

01:14:24.794 --> 01:14:26.921
You don't wanna leave anything unsaid.

01:14:27.505 --> 01:14:28.422
Really?

01:14:28.506 --> 01:14:31.133
Don't hold back now. You'll regret it.

01:14:31.217 --> 01:14:33.761
Leave nothing unsaid.

01:14:40.559 --> 01:14:42.228
I'm sorry. Very.

01:14:52.905 --> 01:14:55.449
I used to whack off
into our vacuum cleaner...

01:14:56.450 --> 01:14:58.452
thinking about Magdalena, our housekeeper.

01:14:59.787 --> 01:15:01.122
And then Mom...

01:15:01.455 --> 01:15:04.542
replaced the vacuum
with one of those Dysons

01:15:05.042 --> 01:15:06.293
that doesn't have a hose.

01:15:09.922 --> 01:15:11.215
And I felt lost.

01:15:11.298 --> 01:15:12.258
[sobs]

01:15:15.261 --> 01:15:16.554
[groans]

01:15:18.764 --> 01:15:23.602
But fortunately, I figured out,
one time after breakfast,

01:15:24.186 --> 01:15:29.859
that if you fill a Ziploc bag
full of Bisquick and warm water,

01:15:30.985 --> 01:15:32.486
and then make a tube...

01:15:33.070 --> 01:15:34.947
He's been in there for an hour.

01:15:35.031 --> 01:15:37.575
I guess he's got a lot on his mind.

01:15:42.038 --> 01:15:43.289
Thank you.

01:15:46.584 --> 01:15:49.628
Whatever happens,
I feel like a weight's been lifted.

01:15:51.047 --> 01:15:52.423
I'm gonna grab a smoke.

01:16:01.098 --> 01:16:05.227
Here is a man who taught us
that you can walk with God,

01:16:06.020 --> 01:16:07.730
even without legs.

01:16:07.813 --> 01:16:12.651
The <i>Navi </i>Shmuel,
in the eponymous Book of Samuel,

01:16:12.735 --> 01:16:15.780
tells the painful story of Mephibosheth,

01:16:15.863 --> 01:16:19.241
the son of Jonathan,
the grandson of King Saul,

01:16:19.325 --> 01:16:22.578
a man who was loyal to King David
through thick and thin.

01:16:22.661 --> 01:16:23.704
[sobbing]

01:16:23.788 --> 01:16:27.583
Mephibosheth, the prophet tells us,
was lame,

01:16:27.666 --> 01:16:30.169
and lived at the mercy
of those around him.

01:16:30.753 --> 01:16:34.548
-He was manipulated, mocked...
-What's with the strip?

01:16:34.632 --> 01:16:35.966
That a Jewish thing?

01:16:37.384 --> 01:16:40.888
I use it to keep me from snoring.
I don't wanna be rude.

01:16:41.680 --> 01:16:44.016
[rabbi] Seymour Lustig was loyal
through and through.

01:16:44.100 --> 01:16:45.601
[praying in Hebrew]

01:16:54.860 --> 01:16:55.945
[snoring lightly]

01:17:04.203 --> 01:17:08.499
The time I was able to spend
with Private Seymour Lustig was brief.

01:17:08.582 --> 01:17:09.458
[snoring]

01:17:09.542 --> 01:17:12.628
But the lessons I learned
will last a lifetime.

01:17:13.546 --> 01:17:16.590
Private Lustig was not
a man of many words,

01:17:16.674 --> 01:17:19.301
but he did tell me
that he loved West Hempstead,

01:17:19.885 --> 01:17:22.847
and even said that I had done a great job.

01:17:23.556 --> 01:17:25.099
[Kenny] You did great up there.

01:17:25.182 --> 01:17:26.183
-Ah, thanks.
-Yeah.

01:17:26.267 --> 01:17:29.812
-Sorry about your loss.
-Thank you. I'll see you tomorrow night.

01:17:29.895 --> 01:17:32.022
No, no, no. That's not happening.

01:17:32.106 --> 01:17:33.107
What's that?

01:17:33.190 --> 01:17:35.901
Why would we have a tribute dinner
if he's not gonna be there?

01:17:35.985 --> 01:17:40.406
Well, I figured a nice
kinda posthumous kinda thing.

01:17:40.489 --> 01:17:42.950
The funeral was a posthumous
kind of thing, no?

01:17:43.033 --> 01:17:46.579
Yeah, but I thought
you already promised us the dinner, so...

01:17:47.872 --> 01:17:50.207
I know about the diabetes, okay?

01:17:50.958 --> 01:17:52.293
All right?

01:17:52.376 --> 01:17:55.963
I think we're done here.
Now, let's put him in the hearse.

01:17:59.884 --> 01:18:00.759
[thudding]

01:18:00.843 --> 01:18:04.054
-Oh. Got to keep it level, man.
-Morons.

01:18:17.735 --> 01:18:20.070
Hey. How's everybody doing?

01:18:20.154 --> 01:18:21.155
[Sarah] Good, Dad.

01:18:21.238 --> 01:18:24.325
Right. Let's get in the car. Come on.

01:18:24.909 --> 01:18:27.995
You didn't have your guys
fix the ballroom leak yet?

01:18:28.787 --> 01:18:31.332
Well, we're back on, so get 'em on it.

01:18:32.124 --> 01:18:33.500
Please stop giggling.

01:18:33.584 --> 01:18:36.795
[Debbie] Kenny, are you ready?
Come on! The rehearsal dinner's at 8:00!

01:18:36.879 --> 01:18:39.298
I know! I'm going downstairs already!

01:18:39.381 --> 01:18:41.133
-[Debbie] Do his tie!
-All right!

01:18:41.217 --> 01:18:42.384
[Sarah] Wow, Dad!

01:18:42.468 --> 01:18:44.345
What? What happened?

01:18:44.428 --> 01:18:46.764
I think I've seen you
in a suit three times:

01:18:46.847 --> 01:18:49.016
my bat mitzvah, my high school graduation,

01:18:49.099 --> 01:18:51.477
and when you took us to the city
to see <i>Phantom.</i>

01:18:51.560 --> 01:18:52.603
Yeah.

01:18:53.437 --> 01:18:55.814
All three times I wore this suit,
by the way.

01:18:55.898 --> 01:18:57.358
It still looks great.

01:19:02.446 --> 01:19:04.657
You're making it all happen, Dad.

01:19:06.116 --> 01:19:08.327
-Yeah.
-[Isaac] Dad! Dad!

01:19:08.410 --> 01:19:10.537
I think I did my tie good.

01:19:10.621 --> 01:19:12.498
[Kenny] Yeah. Hey, it looks fantastic.

01:19:12.581 --> 01:19:15.417
-It's... Let me just touch it up.
-Okay.

01:19:15.501 --> 01:19:17.169
Okay. You knotted it up good.

01:19:17.795 --> 01:19:19.129
Wow, Dr. Cortice.

01:19:19.213 --> 01:19:20.339
So handsome.

01:19:20.422 --> 01:19:22.591
-Everyone's so excited for tonight.
-[Kenny] Come on.

01:19:22.675 --> 01:19:25.427
It's not City Hall,
but we'll have some fun.

01:19:25.511 --> 01:19:27.179
Okay, okay.

01:19:27.263 --> 01:19:29.932
-[grunting]
-[Kenny] Okay.

01:19:30.015 --> 01:19:31.475
Hey, what's wrong?

01:19:31.558 --> 01:19:33.727
Hey. Nothing, pally.

01:19:33.811 --> 01:19:37.356
You look like you found out
Sears went out of business.

01:19:37.439 --> 01:19:39.275
[chuckles] No, no, no.

01:19:41.318 --> 01:19:42.653
Did tomorrow blow up?

01:19:45.155 --> 01:19:47.950
Yeah. Yeah, but it's okay.

01:19:48.951 --> 01:19:51.245
So, your family's good with it?

01:19:51.328 --> 01:19:54.790
I can't...
I haven't had the heart to tell them.

01:19:55.291 --> 01:19:58.502
Look, why don't you just
let me pay for City Hall,

01:19:58.585 --> 01:20:00.004
and nobody has to find out.

01:20:00.587 --> 01:20:03.048
Yeah. Please don't ask again.

01:20:03.132 --> 01:20:04.508
-Okay, I'm sorry.
-Okay.

01:20:04.591 --> 01:20:06.218
-You'll figure it out.
-Thank you.

01:20:06.302 --> 01:20:09.305
Tonight, it's just immediate family.
It's not that big a deal.

01:20:10.347 --> 01:20:11.432
Thanks.

01:20:12.599 --> 01:20:16.228
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!

01:20:16.312 --> 01:20:19.023
I'll say hi to the driver.
That's what I'm gonna do.

01:20:20.691 --> 01:20:22.818
[Isaac] Wait, wait.
Which one are you driving in?

01:20:22.901 --> 01:20:25.321
If they had to drive themselves,
they might get lost.

01:20:25.404 --> 01:20:29.074
Yeah, the Hamptons are hard to find.
That makes sense.

01:20:29.158 --> 01:20:30.701
You got two of 'em, huh?

01:20:30.784 --> 01:20:32.661
Yeah, they gave me two
for the price of two.

01:20:32.745 --> 01:20:35.581
[Kenny chuckles]
That's funny. That's funny.

01:20:38.542 --> 01:20:40.544
[ambient music playing]

01:20:42.880 --> 01:20:44.548
[indistinct chatter]

01:20:45.132 --> 01:20:46.842
Dad, this place is like a dream.

01:20:46.925 --> 01:20:50.637
Oh, yeah. It's very understated,
just like Sarah's taste.

01:20:50.721 --> 01:20:53.307
They've got croissants in a jar and...

01:20:53.390 --> 01:20:56.060
This place is amazing. Who lives here?

01:20:56.143 --> 01:20:58.854
Thank you. It's a well-known celebrity.

01:20:58.937 --> 01:21:01.648
Do you know Psy?
He recorded that song "Gangnam Style."

01:21:01.732 --> 01:21:03.317
You know Psy?

01:21:03.400 --> 01:21:05.569
Well, actually, I did his father's heart.

01:21:05.652 --> 01:21:07.279
He lends his art to museums.

01:21:07.363 --> 01:21:09.948
[Debbie gasps]
Of course he does. Amazing.

01:21:10.032 --> 01:21:12.409
Psy has beautiful taste, doesn't he, Mom?

01:21:14.119 --> 01:21:17.289
Oh. Oh, yeah, wonderful taste. Mmm-hmm.

01:21:18.332 --> 01:21:21.001
You know, when you bite your thumb,
you're supposed to stop.

01:21:29.343 --> 01:21:30.594
How's school?

01:21:31.178 --> 01:21:33.472
Dad, I took a year off to travel abroad.

01:21:34.181 --> 01:21:35.891
Oh, yeah. Yeah, I knew that.

01:21:38.936 --> 01:21:40.270
Did you try the pork dumplings?

01:21:40.354 --> 01:21:41.814
They're so good.

01:21:42.314 --> 01:21:46.402
No, because I'm a vegetarian.
I've been a vegetarian for two years.

01:21:46.485 --> 01:21:48.570
Oh, I thought that was slang
for something.

01:21:48.654 --> 01:21:50.906
No, Dad, I'm not a lesbian.
I keep telling you.

01:21:51.407 --> 01:21:52.991
-You're not?
-[glass clinking]

01:21:53.700 --> 01:21:55.160
Hello, everybody.

01:21:55.994 --> 01:21:59.164
This has been such a gratifying night,
to see all of you

01:21:59.248 --> 01:22:01.417
-enjoying yourselves so much...
-Thank you.

01:22:01.500 --> 01:22:03.043
...after all our planning.

01:22:03.127 --> 01:22:04.044
And to Sarah,

01:22:04.128 --> 01:22:06.839
we can't wait to have you in our family.

01:22:06.922 --> 01:22:07.965
Thank you.

01:22:08.048 --> 01:22:10.676
I can't wait to spoil my first grandchild.

01:22:10.759 --> 01:22:12.594
[all laugh]

01:22:12.678 --> 01:22:16.890
May I add here that we are especially
excited for a Jewish grandchild.

01:22:16.974 --> 01:22:19.768
As you know, Drake is black and Jewish,

01:22:19.852 --> 01:22:22.688
and he's our favorite artist
to make love to.

01:22:23.564 --> 01:22:24.398
Okay.

01:22:24.481 --> 01:22:26.024
Okay, Kirby.

01:22:26.108 --> 01:22:29.611
-Speech from the father!
-Oh! didn't know I was supposed to speak.

01:22:30.195 --> 01:22:31.488
I'll do one if he doesn't.

01:22:31.572 --> 01:22:33.157
No, no, that's okay, kid.

01:22:33.240 --> 01:22:36.243
Uh... Well, what can I say?

01:22:36.326 --> 01:22:39.580
First, I wanna salute my ex-wife, Katrina.

01:22:39.663 --> 01:22:43.542
It's a great speech,
and her boyfriend, Pistachio.

01:22:44.293 --> 01:22:47.713
So, we're here to talk about my son,

01:22:47.796 --> 01:22:49.631
who, uh... You know...

01:22:49.715 --> 01:22:53.802
I wasn't there when he was born,
but I was on my way.

01:22:54.303 --> 01:22:58.182
And when I got there,
I was excited to meet him.

01:22:59.641 --> 01:23:02.060
I never hit my children.

01:23:03.103 --> 01:23:05.939
That's one of the good things
about not being there.

01:23:07.024 --> 01:23:09.067
I never beat their mother.

01:23:10.068 --> 01:23:13.822
She beat me a couple of times.
We called the cops.

01:23:14.656 --> 01:23:18.702
You know what? Let's forget 2008, okay?

01:23:18.785 --> 01:23:20.370
Not even gonna bring it up now.

01:23:26.543 --> 01:23:28.045
Should've let me go.

01:23:45.395 --> 01:23:47.314
[upbeat music playing in distance]

01:23:59.493 --> 01:24:01.495
What the hell are you doing?

01:24:01.578 --> 01:24:05.415
[chuckles] Check it out.
I snuck some video at the bachelor party.

01:24:05.499 --> 01:24:07.459
You're looking at strippers?

01:24:07.543 --> 01:24:09.461
Your father just died today.

01:24:09.545 --> 01:24:11.672
Hey, it's after midnight, okay?
That was yesterday.

01:24:11.755 --> 01:24:12.673
Well...

01:24:13.215 --> 01:24:16.093
Listen, I need your help. I...

01:24:16.176 --> 01:24:18.762
The mayor backed outta the City Hall.

01:24:18.845 --> 01:24:21.765
Politicians. You know they're lying
'cause their lips are moving.

01:24:21.848 --> 01:24:25.143
-I still haven't told anybody yet.
-Well, don't.

01:24:25.227 --> 01:24:26.520
Here's what you say.

01:24:26.603 --> 01:24:29.898
The mayor said something racist to you,
and you had to pull the plug.

01:24:29.982 --> 01:24:31.108
People love that.

01:24:31.191 --> 01:24:32.067
How?

01:24:32.150 --> 01:24:35.445
[stammering] How do you even prove that?

01:24:35.529 --> 01:24:37.322
Fine. How about bats?

01:24:37.406 --> 01:24:38.657
What?

01:24:38.740 --> 01:24:42.119
You say you can't do the wedding there
because there's bats in City Hall.

01:24:42.202 --> 01:24:43.620
You know, an infestation.

01:24:43.704 --> 01:24:46.999
There's bats all around!
In the underpass at the train station.

01:24:47.082 --> 01:24:49.710
All we need is nets. All right?
We get them into City Hall,

01:24:49.793 --> 01:24:51.628
and they have to close it down. Done.

01:24:51.712 --> 01:24:53.213
-What are we getting?
-Bats.

01:24:53.297 --> 01:24:54.673
No-- Stop it!

01:24:54.756 --> 01:24:57.593
-What are you doing up?
-I'm always up. Bats?

01:24:57.676 --> 01:24:59.803
No, I don't know what he's talking about.

01:25:01.680 --> 01:25:05.767
Okay, listen.
The mayor killed the wedding.

01:25:05.851 --> 01:25:07.936
Just... Just 'cause of the lying?

01:25:08.020 --> 01:25:12.274
I don't know how to tell anybody.
I'm sick to my stomach right now.

01:25:12.357 --> 01:25:15.110
So we have to sabotage City Hall!

01:25:16.445 --> 01:25:19.781
Fireplace. Remember? There's a fireplace
in the mayor's office.

01:25:19.865 --> 01:25:23.243
We just get bats down the chimney,
and we're in. That's it.

01:25:23.327 --> 01:25:25.245
Come on.
There's only a few hours of darkness.

01:25:25.829 --> 01:25:29.082
What? You and me are gonna go catch
a bunch of bats?

01:25:29.166 --> 01:25:31.418
And me. I'll help.

01:25:31.501 --> 01:25:34.630
Yeah, but they are fast.
We'll need a bunch of people.

01:25:34.713 --> 01:25:37.591
<i>♪ This is the time to remember ♪</i>

01:25:37.674 --> 01:25:38.634
[bats screeching]

01:25:38.717 --> 01:25:41.845
-[all screaming, grunting]
<i>-♪ 'Cause it will not last forever ♪</i>

01:25:42.429 --> 01:25:46.058
<i>♪ These are the days to hold on to ♪</i>

01:25:46.141 --> 01:25:49.603
<i>♪ 'Cause we won't</i>
<i>Although we'll want to ♪</i>

01:25:49.686 --> 01:25:53.023
<i>♪ This is the time ♪</i>

01:25:53.106 --> 01:25:54.733
<i>♪ But time is gonna change ♪</i>

01:25:55.400 --> 01:25:58.070
Are you sure we don't need
the other guys for this?

01:25:58.153 --> 01:26:01.114
Ah, it's only two floors.
I can scale it myself.

01:26:01.698 --> 01:26:03.033
One...

01:26:03.742 --> 01:26:04.743
two...

01:26:05.786 --> 01:26:07.204
three!

01:26:08.205 --> 01:26:09.414
-[Kenny] Oh!
-[bats screeching]

01:26:09.498 --> 01:26:12.584
Oh, oh, oh! They're freaking out.

01:26:12.668 --> 01:26:15.253
-[Kenny] Ah, come on!
-Calm down.

01:26:16.046 --> 01:26:17.172
Give me the Kahlua.

01:26:17.255 --> 01:26:18.173
The what?

01:26:18.256 --> 01:26:20.384
It's still in the trunk. Come on. Hurry.

01:26:21.968 --> 01:26:23.178
[Kenny grunts]

01:26:25.931 --> 01:26:27.015
You all right?

01:26:27.099 --> 01:26:29.810
-Just hold it steady.
-Careful, careful.

01:26:29.893 --> 01:26:31.687
{\an8}-[Charles] Hold my--
-I got it!

01:26:31.770 --> 01:26:33.146
{\an8}-All right, bag!
-[whimpers]

01:26:33.230 --> 01:26:35.941
{\an8}[Kenny] Bag! Bag! Give it to him!
Get it! Go!

01:26:36.024 --> 01:26:37.359
-[Charles] All right.
-Go.

01:26:37.442 --> 01:26:38.985
[Kenny] Go! Yes!

01:26:39.069 --> 01:26:40.487
-[Kenny] Good, good.
-Yes!

01:26:40.570 --> 01:26:41.905
[Kenny] Go, go.

01:26:41.988 --> 01:26:43.031
[Charles grunts]

01:26:43.115 --> 01:26:44.491
[Kenny] Okay.

01:26:44.574 --> 01:26:46.284
-[Debbie] Oh!
-[Charles grunts]

01:26:47.077 --> 01:26:48.662
-[Debbie] Ah!
-[Charles grunts]

01:26:53.083 --> 01:26:54.042
[bats screech]

01:26:57.754 --> 01:26:59.923
[bats screeching]

01:27:10.308 --> 01:27:11.435
[Kenny] What're you doing?

01:27:11.518 --> 01:27:12.519
[wings fluttering]

01:27:14.521 --> 01:27:16.314
Gotta give it a minute.

01:27:16.398 --> 01:27:18.233
The bats need to know that
they can't fly out.

01:27:21.653 --> 01:27:22.946
[fluttering fades]

01:27:23.029 --> 01:27:24.406
All right, I think we're good.

01:27:24.489 --> 01:27:25.741
[bats screeching]

01:27:26.324 --> 01:27:27.784
What the heck?

01:27:27.868 --> 01:27:29.578
-Oh, my God!
-Oh, my God.

01:27:30.954 --> 01:27:32.831
[woman squealing]

01:27:32.914 --> 01:27:34.624
-Get your clothes!
-I got it!

01:27:34.708 --> 01:27:35.876
Clear!

01:27:36.877 --> 01:27:37.836
[mayor] Let's go.

01:27:39.212 --> 01:27:40.213
[woman] Call 911.

01:27:40.297 --> 01:27:43.425
Go! No 911! Can't do that. Let's just go.

01:27:43.508 --> 01:27:45.343
[tires screeching]

01:27:45.427 --> 01:27:48.388
[Billy Joel's "Scenes
from an Italian Restaurant" playing]

01:27:51.308 --> 01:27:53.560
[mayor and woman exclaiming]

01:27:56.313 --> 01:27:57.814
All right, done!

01:27:59.149 --> 01:28:02.861
Might wanna throw away that bag, though.
Those morons pooped in it.

01:28:08.241 --> 01:28:11.369
<i>Police and animal control are working</i>
<i>to remove several dozen bats</i>

01:28:11.453 --> 01:28:15.624
<i>that were discovered this morning</i>
<i>inside West Hempstead City Hall.</i>

01:28:15.707 --> 01:28:19.211
What the hell?
Kenny, what are we gonna do?

01:28:19.294 --> 01:28:20.962
I don't know. That was crazy.

01:28:21.046 --> 01:28:24.007
You can get all kinds of rabies
from those assholes.

01:28:24.090 --> 01:28:26.009
Are people even gonna wanna go
in there now?

01:28:26.092 --> 01:28:29.179
Honey, I'm sure if you want it there,
most people will go,

01:28:29.262 --> 01:28:31.097
if... If we're allowed.

01:28:31.181 --> 01:28:33.475
-Right?
-I don't know. I don't know.

01:28:33.558 --> 01:28:35.644
Well, don't put this all on yourself,
sweetheart.

01:28:35.727 --> 01:28:38.563
Come on, everybody. Come in here.
Gather 'round.

01:28:39.314 --> 01:28:43.318
Maybe we should take a poll to see where
everyone's heads are at right now.

01:28:43.401 --> 01:28:48.323
Would you rather we bring the wedding
back to the hotel, where the big leak is,

01:28:48.406 --> 01:28:51.326
or City Hall, with the bats?

01:28:51.409 --> 01:28:53.411
Who... Who would rather have the bats?

01:28:58.959 --> 01:29:02.212
I'm pretty sure the bats are
not gonna be good for Noah.

01:29:02.295 --> 01:29:03.839
[news anchor] <i>Pablo, thank you.</i>

01:29:03.922 --> 01:29:07.217
<i>The mayor expressed deep dismay,</i>
<i>saying he heard about this right now,</i>

01:29:07.300 --> 01:29:09.302
<i>and was far away from City Hall</i>
<i>when it happened,</i>

01:29:09.386 --> 01:29:12.848
<i>still mourning the passing of</i>
<i>local war hero Seymour Lustig.</i>

01:29:12.931 --> 01:29:14.933
<i>He said City Hall has been evacuated,</i>

01:29:15.016 --> 01:29:18.687
<i>and will not be reopened until every bat</i>
<i>and every last pellet of bat feces</i>

01:29:18.770 --> 01:29:20.272
<i>has been found and disposed of.</i>

01:29:20.355 --> 01:29:21.606
Ay-ay-ay.

01:29:21.690 --> 01:29:26.111
Well, I guess we'll have to rebook
the hotel if it's still available.

01:29:26.194 --> 01:29:28.113
My wedding is today, Mom.

01:29:28.196 --> 01:29:31.449
Sweetheart, I will get that done for you.
I promise you.

01:29:35.787 --> 01:29:38.540
-[Kenny chuckles softly]
-Aw, Daddy will fix it.

01:29:38.623 --> 01:29:41.710
What can you do? It happens. Bats.

01:29:43.211 --> 01:29:45.213
[indistinct chatter]

01:29:53.597 --> 01:29:55.682
-[rap song playing]
<i>-♪ Tell me where your head's at ♪</i>

01:29:55.765 --> 01:29:58.602
<i>-♪ Are you a one-night stand-- ♪</i>
-[instrumental music playing]

01:30:00.896 --> 01:30:02.898
[singing in Hebrew]

01:30:17.579 --> 01:30:19.289
Powerful shit.

01:30:21.291 --> 01:30:24.169
Powerful, meaningful shit.

01:30:33.178 --> 01:30:35.680
-Whoop! There it is! Ah!
-[guests cheering]

01:30:35.764 --> 01:30:37.057
[Sarah laughs]

01:30:39.517 --> 01:30:43.855
Under the rabbinical authority of
the West Hempstead Synagogue,

01:30:43.939 --> 01:30:46.232
I pronounce you husband and wife.

01:30:48.652 --> 01:30:50.528
-[glass shatters]
-[screams]

01:30:50.612 --> 01:30:51.863
No! No!

01:30:51.947 --> 01:30:53.448
-Breathe. Breathe. Breathe.
-No!

01:30:53.531 --> 01:30:55.659
What you're feeling is scary,
but not dangerous.

01:30:56.368 --> 01:30:57.619
You may kiss.

01:31:02.248 --> 01:31:03.541
[guests cheering and applauding]

01:31:05.919 --> 01:31:07.295
Yes.

01:31:10.799 --> 01:31:12.550
I just broke my heel.

01:31:13.218 --> 01:31:14.052
Yeah.

01:31:20.350 --> 01:31:21.810
She broke her shoe.

01:31:21.893 --> 01:31:24.854
-She broke her shoe.
-Stop. That's not your job anymore.

01:31:24.938 --> 01:31:28.191
-Just let him be the husband.
-Yeah, I know.

01:31:28.775 --> 01:31:30.777
[murmuring and laughing]

01:31:37.325 --> 01:31:39.035
Yeah. Yeah, yeah.

01:31:39.119 --> 01:31:41.121
[indistinct chatter]

01:32:03.435 --> 01:32:05.854
[Kent] Ladies and gentlemen,

01:32:05.937 --> 01:32:08.314
believers and skeptics,

01:32:08.398 --> 01:32:11.443
feast your eyes on the wonder that is...

01:32:11.526 --> 01:32:13.361
the wedding party!

01:32:16.156 --> 01:32:18.700
<i>♪ Just a small-town girl ♪</i>

01:32:19.826 --> 01:32:22.912
<i>♪ Livin' in a lonely world ♪</i>

01:32:24.164 --> 01:32:29.627
<i>♪ She took the midnight train</i>
<i>Going anywhere ♪</i>

01:32:32.547 --> 01:32:39.262
<i>♪ Just a city boy</i>
<i>Born and raised in South Detroit ♪</i>

01:32:40.472 --> 01:32:46.352
<i>♪ He took the midnight train</i>
<i>Going anywhere ♪</i>

01:33:04.287 --> 01:33:05.205
[laughing]

01:33:05.288 --> 01:33:07.582
<i>♪ A singer in a smoky room ♪</i>

01:33:07.665 --> 01:33:08.625
Oh, ooh!

01:33:08.708 --> 01:33:11.753
<i>♪ A smell of wine and cheap perfume ♪</i>

01:33:11.836 --> 01:33:13.254
[all cheering]

01:33:13.838 --> 01:33:16.424
We got us a ghetto wedding.

01:33:19.719 --> 01:33:22.972
<i>♪ Strangers waiting ♪</i>

01:33:24.641 --> 01:33:26.184
<i>♪ Up and down the boulevard ♪</i>

01:33:26.267 --> 01:33:28.144
Yeah. Good pick.

01:33:28.645 --> 01:33:30.855
[traditional Jewish music playing]

01:33:36.653 --> 01:33:37.654
[laughing]

01:33:57.966 --> 01:33:59.968
[all cheering]

01:34:07.976 --> 01:34:09.185
[Sarah yelling and laughing]

01:34:19.112 --> 01:34:21.030
[Katrina and Debbie screaming]

01:34:23.700 --> 01:34:25.493
[exclaiming in disgust]

01:34:35.003 --> 01:34:36.796
You... You're not enjoying this, are you?

01:34:36.880 --> 01:34:38.506
No, no, I'm good.

01:34:39.090 --> 01:34:40.216
You don't look good.

01:34:40.300 --> 01:34:42.635
I mean, me?
I got a reason to be miserable.

01:34:43.344 --> 01:34:44.929
I barely know my own family.

01:34:45.013 --> 01:34:47.140
That's not true. They love you.

01:34:47.223 --> 01:34:49.809
They gotta love me.
I... I write the checks.

01:34:49.893 --> 01:34:51.686
You? Your wife loves you.

01:34:51.769 --> 01:34:52.979
Your kids love you.

01:34:53.062 --> 01:34:56.232
My kids love you.
Shit! My... My whole family loves you.

01:34:56.316 --> 01:34:58.193
Pally, why do you think...

01:34:58.276 --> 01:35:02.280
Oh, oh, guys, we're... We're talking.
Can you please just lift us back up?

01:35:03.114 --> 01:35:06.826
Why do you think they give you grief,
your kids? Because they love you!

01:35:06.910 --> 01:35:09.746
It's different.
You were there when they needed you.

01:35:09.829 --> 01:35:11.080
I was chasing ass.

01:35:11.164 --> 01:35:13.708
Now, where...
Where did all this ass come from?

01:35:13.791 --> 01:35:16.836
I was a young black surgeon in LA.

01:35:16.920 --> 01:35:19.964
It was like I was Dr. Denzel for 30 years.

01:35:20.048 --> 01:35:22.759
Okay. Okay, guys, guys.
I said we were still talking. Hold up.

01:35:22.842 --> 01:35:24.135
Please. Come on, pally.

01:35:24.219 --> 01:35:27.096
Still plenty of time
to make it up to them.

01:35:27.180 --> 01:35:28.765
Plenty of time?

01:35:28.848 --> 01:35:32.435
I don't know about you, but this
kinda seems like the final act to me.

01:35:32.518 --> 01:35:36.439
No, no, no. This is just the start
of the next phase.

01:35:36.522 --> 01:35:40.693
Yeah, right! You look real psyched
about this next phase.

01:35:40.777 --> 01:35:42.070
What, I'm not psyched?

01:35:42.987 --> 01:35:44.781
-Come on!
-Hey! Whoa, whoa!

01:35:44.864 --> 01:35:46.866
You kiddin' me? The man's talkin', here!

01:35:46.950 --> 01:35:49.118
I can't hold it anymore. Talk down here.

01:35:49.202 --> 01:35:52.664
It's a private conversation.
Come on, 30 more seconds.

01:35:52.747 --> 01:35:54.040
I'm not psyched?

01:35:54.123 --> 01:35:55.291
You know what, pal?

01:35:56.084 --> 01:36:00.004
If I had dedicated my whole life
to my kids the way you did,

01:36:00.088 --> 01:36:02.507
I'd be scared to face tomorrow, too.

01:36:04.717 --> 01:36:05.718
[Sarah] Dad.

01:36:05.802 --> 01:36:08.012
Dad, get the hell down!
Uncle Mark's gonna collapse!

01:36:08.096 --> 01:36:10.431
-What's that?
-[Mark] Damn it.

01:36:10.515 --> 01:36:11.975
[all shouting]

01:36:16.521 --> 01:36:18.690
[indistinct shouting]

01:36:27.198 --> 01:36:28.408
[man] Save the veil!

01:36:34.831 --> 01:36:36.416
There's sprinklers.

01:36:37.333 --> 01:36:38.543
[hisses]

01:36:38.626 --> 01:36:39.961
Were sprinklers.

01:36:40.586 --> 01:36:42.255
[Hanan laughing hysterically]

01:36:50.179 --> 01:36:51.514
Where is the...

01:36:51.597 --> 01:36:54.309
-Are you okay, babe?
-Yeah. Where's Sarah?

01:36:54.892 --> 01:36:56.811
Dad! Daddy, are you all right?

01:36:56.894 --> 01:36:58.438
I'm fine. I need to talk to you.

01:36:58.521 --> 01:37:00.773
I need to... Come here. I'll be, uh...

01:37:00.857 --> 01:37:02.817
Gimme a minute. Just, everyone go.

01:37:05.486 --> 01:37:06.321
[shrieks]

01:37:07.488 --> 01:37:10.241
-I love you.
-I know. Let's just get out of here.

01:37:10.325 --> 01:37:11.826
I love you. I'm sorry.

01:37:12.577 --> 01:37:14.537
Dad. I know how hard you worked.

01:37:14.620 --> 01:37:16.622
-I had to pay for it.
-You did everything you could.

01:37:16.706 --> 01:37:17.999
-I know.
-No.

01:37:18.082 --> 01:37:21.377
I... I should've let Tyler's dad help pay,

01:37:22.128 --> 01:37:23.838
instead of being a big shot.

01:37:24.422 --> 01:37:27.508
I... I had to make the whole thing
about me.

01:37:31.179 --> 01:37:32.972
Instead of, uh... [sniffles]

01:37:34.015 --> 01:37:36.059
...just the wedding. I just...

01:37:36.142 --> 01:37:38.686
[stammering] I didn't wanna
have to think about...

01:37:39.896 --> 01:37:41.230
About what, Dad?

01:37:42.607 --> 01:37:43.691
About...

01:37:45.401 --> 01:37:46.402
[smacks lips]

01:37:47.445 --> 01:37:50.323
This is the last thing
I'm ever gonna get to do for you.

01:37:51.407 --> 01:37:52.533
I'm losin' you.

01:37:53.993 --> 01:37:55.620
[sobbing] Dad, you're not.

01:37:55.703 --> 01:38:02.085
[sobbing] Yeah, no, I am. I am. It's okay.
It's how it works. It's a crappy system.

01:38:03.378 --> 01:38:05.213
But he's such a good kid.

01:38:05.296 --> 01:38:07.298
He's the best, and I'm sorry.

01:38:07.382 --> 01:38:11.761
And I'm sorry to both of you guys.
You deserve better than what I gave you.

01:38:12.220 --> 01:38:15.681
I love you so much. Thank you.

01:38:16.432 --> 01:38:18.476
Thank you for saying that.

01:38:19.477 --> 01:38:24.440
You'll never lose me.
And I'll take you over any fancy place.

01:38:28.820 --> 01:38:31.906
Come on, you guys. We gotta get going.

01:38:31.989 --> 01:38:34.325
What? All right, where's the fire exit?

01:38:34.409 --> 01:38:36.536
No, we gotta take the wedding pictures.

01:38:36.619 --> 01:38:40.248
-Are you insane?
-No, they found a room without a fire.

01:38:40.331 --> 01:38:41.791
Sir, we'll get it done quickly.

01:38:41.874 --> 01:38:44.335
[Kenny sobbing loudly]

01:38:46.254 --> 01:38:48.423
Can you guys get it together?

01:38:48.506 --> 01:38:50.716
Okay, yeah, absolutely.

01:38:50.800 --> 01:38:51.843
I'm sorry, uh...

01:38:52.593 --> 01:38:54.137
Just give me one more try.

01:38:55.054 --> 01:38:56.472
[Kenny sobbing]

01:38:56.556 --> 01:38:57.473
[camera clicking]

01:38:59.308 --> 01:39:00.351
[both sobbing]

01:39:03.438 --> 01:39:05.940
I don't think I've ever seen
Dad cry before.

01:39:06.023 --> 01:39:07.567
Mike Piazza's retirement.

01:39:09.485 --> 01:39:10.611
[Kenny and Kirby sobbing]

01:39:11.779 --> 01:39:13.781
[electronic music playing]

01:39:15.241 --> 01:39:16.576
[indistinct chatter]

01:39:20.746 --> 01:39:23.624
-[Kenny] Come on, guys. We'll put it here.
-[man] Where's it go?

01:39:24.208 --> 01:39:26.544
[Kenny] Take 'er down. Take it.
Take it. There.

01:39:31.132 --> 01:39:36.471
All right, come on. You wanna turn. Yup.
We got the brakes. This way!

01:39:36.554 --> 01:39:38.014
[indistinct chatter]

01:39:38.097 --> 01:39:40.683
I got three plates.
Here we go! Here we go!

01:39:43.102 --> 01:39:45.188
[guests exclaim and cheer]

01:39:53.988 --> 01:39:56.991
<i>♪ Baby, I think about you</i>
<i>And I feel it ♪</i>

01:39:57.074 --> 01:39:59.869
Hey, come on. Get some of this.

01:40:02.330 --> 01:40:05.541
<i>♪ Maybe we just ain't</i>
<i>Meant to be something ♪</i>

01:40:05.625 --> 01:40:07.627
<i>♪ Maybe we are? ♪</i>

01:40:11.839 --> 01:40:14.550
Hey, how's it goin'?
Lookin' good. Lookin' good.

01:40:14.634 --> 01:40:17.595
Hey, look who made it, man! You made it!

01:40:17.678 --> 01:40:18.888
Just roll with it.

01:40:18.971 --> 01:40:22.141
-Hey, what's up?
-All right, good to see you, man.

01:40:22.225 --> 01:40:23.726
Thanks for having us.

01:40:24.393 --> 01:40:28.773
Sir, I see you really love your queens.
[laughs]

01:40:29.690 --> 01:40:30.733
Big laugh.

01:40:32.235 --> 01:40:33.945
Ladies and gentlemen,

01:40:34.028 --> 01:40:35.780
boys and girls of all ages,

01:40:35.863 --> 01:40:38.533
the time is nigh.

01:40:38.616 --> 01:40:41.202
Watch and marvel

01:40:41.285 --> 01:40:45.081
as the bride and groom partake
in their first dance.

01:40:50.836 --> 01:40:54.757
Sarah, 23 years ago,
your great-grandmother Yetta,

01:40:54.840 --> 01:40:56.384
recorded this

01:40:56.467 --> 01:40:57.718
just for this night,

01:40:58.386 --> 01:41:00.555
knowing she would most certainly be dead.

01:41:02.807 --> 01:41:04.016
Cue video.

01:41:07.228 --> 01:41:12.024
<i>This is for my little Sarah.</i>
<i>May you have a blessed marriage.</i>

01:41:12.108 --> 01:41:14.819
That's... That's the woman in the painting
I said looks like you.

01:41:14.902 --> 01:41:17.238
No. I don't know
what you're talking about.

01:41:18.239 --> 01:41:22.785
<i>♪ When I fall in love ♪</i>

01:41:24.120 --> 01:41:29.917
<i>♪ It will be forever ♪</i>

01:41:30.418 --> 01:41:37.133
<i>♪ Or I'll never fall in love ♪</i>

01:41:37.216 --> 01:41:39.218
[guests cheer and applaud]

01:41:45.516 --> 01:41:50.938
And now, moms and dads,
join us in this wondrous ritual.

01:42:08.414 --> 01:42:09.915
[coughing]

01:42:13.252 --> 01:42:16.631
-That's a good boy you raised there.
-You helped.

01:42:17.548 --> 01:42:19.216
You did about eighty percent.

01:42:19.300 --> 01:42:20.718
Eighty-five.

01:42:23.471 --> 01:42:25.806
-You're a good woman.
-Thank you.

01:42:25.890 --> 01:42:27.808
And I love taking care of you.

01:42:28.768 --> 01:42:31.020
And I love taking care of Ignacio.

01:42:31.103 --> 01:42:33.356
He's like a foreign kid I get to sponsor.

01:42:33.439 --> 01:42:35.149
[both chuckle]

01:42:35.232 --> 01:42:37.652
[Kirby] Hey, Ignacio,
come and take your queen.

01:42:38.944 --> 01:42:40.946
I'm gonna find my princess.

01:43:07.765 --> 01:43:10.685
Did I tell you I love you this week?
Because I do.

01:43:10.768 --> 01:43:13.729
Uh, you might've said it a couple times.

01:43:13.813 --> 01:43:16.273
Ah, less than usual.
That's... That's not right.

01:43:16.357 --> 01:43:18.359
Are you happy? Or just drunk?

01:43:18.442 --> 01:43:22.822
Ah! Both. I don't know.
This is just perfect.

01:43:23.406 --> 01:43:27.993
Oh, and the drizzled peanut brittle
was incredible.

01:43:28.077 --> 01:43:32.665
Oh. You're not just saying that?
[smacks lips] Oh.

01:43:33.541 --> 01:43:36.711
Mmm. Totally worth the salmonella.

01:43:36.794 --> 01:43:37.753
[Debbie laughs]

01:43:37.837 --> 01:43:38.838
[Kent] And now,

01:43:38.921 --> 01:43:43.134
join us as we welcome in that most tender
of traditions,

01:43:43.217 --> 01:43:45.928
the father-daughter dance.

01:43:46.887 --> 01:43:48.889
[guests cheer]

01:43:53.060 --> 01:43:55.813
-[Kenny speaks inaudibly]
-[Tyler laughs]

01:43:57.189 --> 01:43:59.191
We never picked a song. I... I...

01:43:59.775 --> 01:44:00.860
I've got you.

01:44:05.322 --> 01:44:07.450
[Billy Joel's "Lullabye" playing]

01:44:16.333 --> 01:44:19.336
You went with Billy Joel,
even though I was a--

01:44:19.420 --> 01:44:22.673
Yeah, even when...
<i>♪ You had to be a big shot ♪</i>

01:44:23.174 --> 01:44:24.508
Very good.

01:44:25.634 --> 01:44:28.179
You weren't making fun
of Billy Joel there, were you?

01:44:28.262 --> 01:44:29.930
No, Dad, just you.

01:44:30.014 --> 01:44:32.641
-Ah. That's okay.
-Yeah.

01:44:36.437 --> 01:44:41.525
<i>♪ I think you know what</i>
<i>I've been trying to say ♪</i>

01:44:42.318 --> 01:44:48.032
<i>♪ I promised I would never leave you ♪</i>

01:44:48.115 --> 01:44:54.288
<i>♪ And you should always know ♪</i>

01:44:54.371 --> 01:44:56.832
<i>♪ Wherever you may go ♪</i>

01:44:56.916 --> 01:44:59.752
<i>♪ No matter where you are ♪</i>

01:44:59.835 --> 01:45:06.175
<i>♪ I never will be far away ♪</i>

01:45:06.258 --> 01:45:12.515
<i>♪ Good night, my angel</i>
<i>Now it's time to sleep ♪</i>

01:45:12.598 --> 01:45:18.813
<i>♪ And still so many things I want to say ♪</i>

01:45:18.896 --> 01:45:25.152
<i>♪ Remember all the songs you sang for me ♪</i>

01:45:25.236 --> 01:45:31.200
<i>♪ When we went sailing on an emerald bay ♪</i>

01:45:31.283 --> 01:45:37.206
<i>♪ And like a boat out on the ocean ♪</i>

01:45:37.289 --> 01:45:42.753
<i>♪ I'm rocking you to sleep ♪</i>

01:45:43.629 --> 01:45:49.844
<i>♪ The water's dark</i>
<i>And deep inside this ancient heart ♪</i>

01:45:49.927 --> 01:45:56.225
<i>♪ You'll always be a part of me ♪</i>

01:46:02.982 --> 01:46:09.446
<i>♪ Someday we'll all be gone</i>
<i>But lullabies go on and on ♪</i>

01:46:09.947 --> 01:46:12.491
<i>♪ They never die ♪</i>

01:46:12.575 --> 01:46:17.413
<i>♪ That's how you</i>
<i>And I ♪</i>

01:46:17.496 --> 01:46:21.667
<i>♪ Will be ♪</i>

01:46:21.750 --> 01:46:22.710
[gasps]

01:46:22.793 --> 01:46:26.046
-I'm sorry. I guess I miss my dad.
-Mmm-hmm.

01:46:26.130 --> 01:46:28.090
You used to grope your dad's ass?

01:46:28.883 --> 01:46:30.050
You're sick.

01:46:32.511 --> 01:46:33.888
[grunting]

01:46:40.811 --> 01:46:42.104
[doorbell rings]

01:46:51.697 --> 01:46:52.865
You're not at the party.

01:46:52.948 --> 01:46:55.409
-You're not drunk.
-I'm not drunk.

01:46:59.622 --> 01:47:04.293
I'm just staying here with my parents
till I find a place that I like.

01:47:04.376 --> 01:47:06.670
-Uh-huh. Where's your room?
-Upstairs.

01:47:07.254 --> 01:47:11.842
Give me, like, 30 seconds to clean up,
and then I'll, uh...

01:47:19.892 --> 01:47:23.103
<i>♪ You are the best thing ♪</i>

01:47:23.187 --> 01:47:24.438
<i>♪ Yeah, yeah ♪</i>

01:47:25.522 --> 01:47:29.026
<i>♪ You are the best thing ♪</i>

01:47:29.109 --> 01:47:31.111
<i>♪ Yeah, yeah, yeah ♪</i>

01:47:31.195 --> 01:47:33.989
<i>♪ You are the best thing ♪</i>

01:47:34.073 --> 01:47:35.950
♪<i> Ah, na, na, na, na, na, na, na ♪</i>

